{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level","id":938911,"title":"Antedeluvian power level","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-28T09:49:40-07:00","id":938911,"title":"Antedeluvian power level","content":"How powerful are yours?<br /> <br /> What can they do?<br /> <br /> What CAN'T they do?<br /> <br /> And what does it take to kill one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:44:43-07:00","id":938939,"title":"","content":"In my games, they are powerful enough that it takes 13 4th generation vampires to bind them, and they have to be supported by 169 ghouls that they have specially trained. The Antediluvians have perfect immortality. If killed, they will reform within a thousand years. If diabolorized, they will take control of their attacker within a century (Cappadocious is an exception because he wanted to become God and found, too late, that God does not exist, at least not on any level that an Antediluvian can access). The only way to stop them is to ritually imprison them with the previously mentioned ritual, body and soul, after draining them completely of Vitae and staking them. Even then, they will eventually escape after ten thousand years (or sooner, if anyone bothers the iron wrapped tungsten coffins that my NPCs used to prevent the Week of Nightmares).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:46:44-07:00","id":938941,"title":"","content":"I actually don't use them.....lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:55:37-07:00","id":938949,"title":"","content":"They're plot devices. They can do whatever they need to for your story. They can't do anything that ruins your story. To kill them, you have to do the story at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:13:32-07:00","id":938962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=938949#post938949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're plot devices. They can do whatever they need to for your story. They can't do anything that ruins your story. To kill them, you have to do the story at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Also, adding on that in the modern nights, I usually treat 4th and 5ths Gens this way as well. That's how the books treated most of their 4th Gens anyways (Baba Yaga and Ur-Shulgi come to mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:53:34-07:00","id":938990,"title":"","content":"I generally make it so Antedeluvians aren't as godlike as they appear to be. A 10,000 year old Antedeluvian is about twice as powerful as the 5,000 year old Menele and Helena, which means that they're all but invincible to your typical coterie of PCs but aren't omnipotent by any stretch of the imagination. Archmages, Werewolf packs, and so on are all capable of bringing them down as well as sufficiently prepped Sabbat packs (anti-dominate/presence wards and so on).<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if the Antedeluvians were able to awaken from Torpor, they would be dramatically weakened and would require dozens of vampires of low generation or hundreds of high generaton in order to regain their full strength so most don't bother. Instead, they use Dominate 5/Auspex 5 combinations to possess their progeny in order to experience the world and manipulate things through proxies and proxies while lying inert in their tombs. They really don't want to wake up and see no point in it for the most part.<br /> <br /> As a result, this means Methuselah are actually pretty much Antedeluvian lites in my game. In the words of Falcon, they can do everything an Antedeluvian can but slower. Menele, Helena, and Ur-Shulgi are the ancestors of most modern vampires so facing them is effectively like facing an Antedeluvian anyway. Likewise, they're entirely capable of killing their sires and draining their blood just like Neonates are with regular elders--and that's if the Antedeluvians are at full strength.<br /> <br /> So if you ever want a &quot;Gehenna/Fight the Clan Founder&quot; game then I use a 4th generation and make it known modern technology makes it possible to fight them.<br /> <br /> One epic game I played was essentially a Mage/Vampire Chronicle version of <b>Alan Wake</b> by Remedy which dealt with a monstrous darkness which possessed human beings by the hundreds and turned them into monsters until the PCs used the Maguffins to led it into a door through the sun (and one PC sacrificing themselves). Only after the game did I reveal they'd destroyed the Lasombra Antedeluvian.<br /> <br /> I had a similar handling of The Week of Nightmares with credit to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>. In my <b>Week of Nightmares</b>, it was a terrifying monstrous event which got 100,000 people killed in India as well as Bodhivisatas, hundreds of Stargazers, and so on but the Camarilla and Technocracy managed to handle it together. Ravnos put proof to lie the Antedeluvians CAN'T take over the world as godkings but have to move subtly through pawns and catspaws. Even then, no one can tell whether it was Ravnos or Hazimel because bot are roughly powerful enough to have pulled something like this off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2019, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:02:38-07:00","id":939163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=938990#post938990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally make it so Antedeluvians aren't as godlike as they appear to be. A 10,000 year old Antedeluvian is about twice as powerful as the 5,000 year old Menele and Helena, which means that they're all but invincible to your typical coterie of PCs but aren't really omnipotent by any stretch of the imagination. Archmages, Werewolf packs, and so on are all capable of bringing them down as well as sufficiently prepped Sabbat packs (wards and so on).<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if the Antedeluvians were able to awaken from Torpor, they would be dramatically weakened and would require dozens of vampires of low generation or hundreds of high generaton in order to regain their full strength so most don't bother. Instead, they use Dominate 5/Auspex 5 combinations to possess their progeny in order to experience the world and manipulate things through proxies and proxies while lying inert in their tombs. They really don't want to wake up and see no point in it for the most part.<br /> <br /> As a result, this means Methuselah are actually pretty much Antedeluvian lites in my game. In the words of Falcon, they do everything an Antedeluvian can but slower. Menele, Helena, and Ur-Shulgi are the ancestors of most modern vampires so facing them is effectively like facing an Antedeluvian anyway. Likewise, they're entirely capable of killing their sires and draining their blood just like Neonates are with regular elders--and that's if the Antedeluvians are at full strength.<br /> <br /> So if you ever want a &quot;Gehenna/Fight the Clan Founder&quot; game then I use a 4th generation and make it known modern technology makes it possible to fight them.<br /> <br /> One epic game I played was essentially a Mage/Vampire Chronicle version of <b>Alan Wake</b> by Remedy which dealt with a monstrous darkness which possessed human beings by the hundreds and turned them into monsters until the PCs used the Maguffins to led it into a door through the sun (and one PC sacrificing themselves). Only after the game did I reveal they'd destroyed the Lasombra Antedeluvian.<br /> <br /> I had a similar handling of The Week of Nightmares with credit to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>. In my <b>Week of Nightmares</b>, it was a terrifying monstrous event which got 100,000 people killed in India as well as Bodhivisatas, hundreds of Stargazers, and so on but the Camarilla and Technocracy managed to handle it together. Ravnos put proof to lie the Antedeluvians CAN'T take over the world as godkings but have to move subtly through pawns and catspaws. Even then, no one can tell whether it was Ravnos or Hazmiel because bot are roughly powerful enough to have pulled something like this off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the same here. I always treated them as ridiculously powerful ancient vampires (in relation to the average PC), yes, but walking bloodgods? No. They're beatable, especially for well-prepared methuselahs and other upper-level splats. They're absolutely on-par with the strongest beings in the setting, but aren't invincible. I always found the notion of an insurmountable power gap between 4th and 5th gen methuselahs and antes a bit annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:32:31-07:00","id":939187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939163#post939163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much the same here. I always treated them as ridiculously powerful ancient vampires (in relation to the average PC), yes, but walking bloodgods? No. They're beatable, especially for well-prepared methuselahs and other upper-level splats. They're absolutely on-par with the strongest beings in the setting, but aren't invincible. I always found the notion of an insurmountable power gap between 4th and 5th gen methuselahs and antes a bit annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also notably interested in the idea of the Cyclical Gehenna and the idea of more than 13 clans. If I ever feel the need, I may state there's something like 52 3rd generation and plenty of Methuselah have actually ascended to that status or destroyed the old to seize their power.<br /> <br /> Not that anyone would ever know.<br /> <br /> But yes, I dislike the idea 4th generation shouldn't be an Antedeluvian in all but name. It's like 9th to 8th generation. No, it's not as good but it should be damned close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:52:50-07:00","id":939193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939187#post939187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm also notably interested in the idea of the Cyclical Gehenna and the idea of more than 13 clans. If I ever feel the need, I may state there's something like 52 3rd generation and plenty of Methuselah have actually ascended to that status or destroyed the old to seize their power.<br /> <br /> Not that anyone would ever know.<br /> <br /> But yes, I dislike the idea 4th generation shouldn't be an Antedeluvian in all but name. It's like 9th to 8th generation. No, it's not as good but it should be damned close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with all of that.<br /> <br /> The cyclical Gehenna also get me interested, I hope WW'l keep that idea in the new ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:58:37-07:00","id":939196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939193#post939193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree with all of that.<br /> <br /> The cyclical Gehenna also get me interested, I hope WW'l keep that idea in the new ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm torn honestly about the idea because while I love Caine and the origin story of vampires, I'm also tempted that Caine is actually just the vampire who was there at the end of the last Gehenna.<br /> <br /> And Vampires could be closer to fifty or a hundred thousand years old.<br /> <br /> Perhaps even predating humanity.<br /> <br /> Are the Nosferatu, perhaps, the original undead from Pre-human Lovecraftian races?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of weird places you can go with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-28-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T16:13:03-07:00","id":939208,"title":"","content":"1.I generally just make them a lateral step above methusela. Just as a methusela can use presence to charm a city (about 500,000 or less people, like Denver Colorado), a an ante could charm a large metropolis(between san antonio(1,000,000 people) and tokyo(13,000,000 people)). <br /> <br /> 2.Ante's are also limited to 10 powers per discipline(one for each dot), but are able to create combo disciplines with the one they specialize in(&quot;Ventrue&quot; would specialize in dominat combo's, &quot;Toriador&quot;/Ariel would use presence, Etc.).<br /> <br /> 3.They can store an unlimited amount of blood, but they all have methusela's thirst, and are always &quot;Blood starved&quot;(regardless of how much blood they drink, they role frenzy as if they have 1BP). <br /> <br /> 4.I use the &quot;Traits above 5&quot; optional rules from mummy(this applies to all vamps in my games). Only supernatural creatures have attribute traits above 5, so each dot above 5 has it's own passive effect.(6-10 in dexterity adds 1 extra physical action per turn(like running, dodging or attacking), Wits does the same only for mental tasks(like reading, solving enigmas, or hacking a computer, the 7th dot of strength grants lethal to all brawl, etc.)<br /> <br /> 5. They can only be permanently killed by Fire, sunlight, or faith/holy magic(all other sources put them in torpor), but they take double damage(before soak) from these sources.(diablerie doesn't kill them either, and at any time they can choose to try and take over their new host body.)<br /> <br /> 6. gen 3 and up are all limited to 10 in traits, only difference is caine is only torpored by fire/sun/holy and the attacker is hit with any damage dealt to him(before soak) times 7(like the 7 fold curse placed on him in the bible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T16:35:04-07:00","id":939211,"title":"","content":"For me, they're walking blood gods, but their power is so great and their blood so potent that they are almost perpetually locked in torpor and forced to act through proxies. Some of them have thoughts and minds that are thoroughly divorced from humanity, thinking more like animals or aliens. Others, however, have managed to cling quite hard to their humanity. While some are malevolent and seek to destroy all lesser Kindred and basically enslave humanity, others seek goals that would give the impression of an orange or blue morality. There's a couple, however, that might actually be benevolent and fair. They're all, however, still so damn lethargic. Their bodies have grown so powerful that they can't feasibly contain the power within those bodies well anymore. Does God have a physical body? Nope. Acts through proxies (angels and the like). Same deal here, just on a smaller scale.<br /> <br /> As Telgar said, they're plot devices. I really don't use them much at all though. In fact, they could very well just be boogeymen stories that the Sabbat buy into completely. Caine isn't real, the Antes are just figments of their imagination. A clever trick some ancient Malkavian or Nosferatu pulled long ago. Maybe it's something created long ago to allow someone power and influence over other Kindred, giving rise to the Sabbat. Whatever the case is, to me, they're plot devices. If they're real and super powered, it either needs to be a Cthulhu-esque potential bad ending that the PCs need to avert, or their torpor and other opposing Antediluvians keep them in check, hence their insanely complicated chess game they play between each other. Hell, maybe they are so powerful that they actually just don't care anymore and only screw around with their direct Childer, watching as their Grand-Childer get bullied around and manipulated, and seeing how that totem pole reacts.<br /> <br /> I do admit I like some of the other ideas floating around here, but I just like being able to say that &quot;It's an Antediluvian. Call the Justice League.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T16:46:09-07:00","id":939215,"title":"","content":"Awesome ideas <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6383\" data-vbnamecard=\"6383\">Prometheas</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939208#post939208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.I generally just make them a lateral step above methusela. Just as a methusela can use presence to charm a city (about 500,000 or less people, like Denver Colorado), a an ante could charm a large metropolis(between san antonio(1,000,000 people) and tokyo(13,000,000 people)).</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally make &quot;Discipline 10&quot; powerful but not invincible. Augustus Giovanni's Dominate 10 power in my games is he can dominate any member of his mortal family bloodline automatically. Which is a useful but not automatically perfect yet goes a long way to explaining his obsession with family purity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.Ante's are also limited to 10 powers per discipline(one for each dot), but are able to create combo disciplines with the one they specialize in(&quot;Ventrue&quot; would specialize in dominat combo's, &quot;Toriador&quot;/Ariel would use presence, Etc.). </div> </div> </div>Oooo, good one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3.They can store an unlimited amount of blood, but they all have methusela's thirst, and are always &quot;Blood starved&quot;(regardless of how much blood they drink, they role frenzy as if they have 1BP). </div> </div> </div>I tend to rule the reason the antedeluvians need to diablerize their descendants is it's the only way to restore their strength after long torpor. Even then, normal vampires would do but they can dominate their bloodlines near perfectly and it helps charge &quot;their&quot; disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4.I use the &quot;Traits above 5&quot; optional rules from mummy(this applies to all vamps in my games). Only supernatural creatures have attribute traits above 5, so each dot above 5 has it's own passive effect.(6-10 in dexterity adds 1 extra physical action per turn(like running, dodging or attacking), Wits does the same only for mental tasks(like reading, solving enigmas, or hacking a computer, the 7th dot of strength grants lethal to all brawl, etc.) </div> </div> </div>I always liked those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. They can only be permanently killed by Fire, sunlight, or faith/holy magic(all other sources put them in torpor), but they take double damage(before soak) from these sources.(diablerie doesn't kill them either, and at any time they can choose to try and take over their new host body.) </div> </div> </div>I actually had a couple of fun additions to the Antes and their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Cappadocius</b>: I diverge from canon and state Cappadocius actually did diablerize God. Just not the Hebrew God but one of the Exarchs from Requiem. He now rules the Underworld Labyrinths as &quot;Death.&quot;<br /> <br /> Augustus is far far weaker than most Methuselah and would die horribly at the hands of the Capuchin, Lamia, or most other ancient Methuselah.<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b>: Saulot survived by letting his soul be diablerized but he REALLY didn't see Tremere coming and couldn't defend himself if he wanted to because 1,000 year old Archmage w/ Willpower 10 and defensive charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b> was fully confident of his ability to defeat the Anarchs and take them over with his powers so he didn't make any effort to defend himself. However, he didn't expect the Anarchs to SHARE his blood and soul (because he's a selfish prick of the highest order) so the fourteen or so Anarchs who participated divided his power between them and thus prevented Lasombra from taking over any of them.<br /> <br /> He was later resurrected by a foolish mage after centuries of failed attempts by Moncada to piece him back together before being killed again by my mage PCs.<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce</b> was incredibly bored with the prospect of being diablerized, so he just spontaneously generated a 4th generation body full of power for the diablerists to enjoy the strength of then went back to working on surviving the destruction of Earth and the Heat-Death of the universe. It was possibly Yorak's original body since his mind had joined the Tzimisce gestalt.<br /> <br /> Lambach is, notably, possibly 3rd generation and Tzimisce himself--just an avatar of him gathering information.<br /> <br /> <b>Set</b> died at the hands of werewolves. It's an ignominous but very true end for the one Cainite who thought he was a God.<br /> <br /> <b>Osiris</b> the 14th Antedeluvian was either embraced by Irad or Set himself. Dead at Set's hands.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b> is dead at Troile's hands. He was actually kind of a shit leader too and everything we attribute to Ventrue as a clan comes from Mithras and Tiamat.<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b>: Was the first Brujah but she killed plenty of other 3rd generations you've now forgotten.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> is dead-dead. Nuking from orbit was the only way to be sure. The sunlight just finished the job. However, it's an in-universe debate Hazimel was killed instead since the difference between the two would be negligible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-09-2019, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:27:57-07:00","id":939285,"title":"","content":"There is some speculation that there were originally 36 Antediluvians, though 23 of them did not survive long enough to produce a Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:44:44-07:00","id":939293,"title":"","content":"I don't use the Antedeluvians as active components in my chronicles. I only use them for historical event explanation, and to lay out a very general idea of the Jyhad so it provides structure to the politics and events happening in the setting.<br /> <br /> The antedeluvians were in torpor for much of recorded history. I had Cappadocious as the most active (since his actions are just too important to the backstory of the Cappadocians and therefore the Giovanni). In order to make any future Gehenna truly terrifying, I had his three partial awakenings from torpor all coincide with plague epidemics. I thought that it was appropriate the founder of the Clan of Death be associated (caused?) with mass death. I wanted to associate an antedeluvian rising with the idea of terrible calamities that would inaugur the end of the world. The first was during the Plague of Cyprian around AD 250 when the antedeluvian was converted to Christianity. The second was the Plague of Justinian around AD 541 when the Feast of Folly occurred. The last was during the Black Death. The association of Cappadocious' rising with great plagues that imperil humanity is one reason the Camarilla elders looked askance at the Giovanni purge of the rest of their clan mates.<br /> <br /> None of the other antedeluvians were active during the historical period. They've been in torpor or dead since before 3000 BC. Any rumors of their activity, particular with Set, is actually caused by one of their first childer, 4th generation methuselahs of extreme age and power. Prior to that, the antedeluvians were the old god-kings of the Mesopotamian city state legends although a few wandered off to other areas (Set, Ravnos, Saulot). (The Second City was Babel).<br /> <br /> There is a throw away line in the Vampire corebook that the Ventrue antedeluvian is known to be destroyed. That clan is the only one not manipulated by its antedeluvian, and therefore this is the main historical reason the clan is trusted enough to be the traditional leaders among the vampires. I push this heavily. Neonates don't care or don't believe, but I have the NPC elders make cryptic references to that every now and again so the PCs know this is what all or most of the elders actually believe.<br /> <br /> The historical destruction/diablerie of several antedeluvians during the Middle Ages are all essentially faked no matter how successful they seemed to be.<br /> <br /> For the structure of the Jyhad, I had to determine which were truly destroyed and which weren't. Then I had to figure out what each of the survivors wanted in broad terms, and how the setting backstory worked with it. Although I must admit I have not given it much though. I have no details only broad outlines. Usually, it's not important at all. However, if some PC really wanted to investigate the Jyhad, I have at least an idea of where to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:02:15-07:00","id":939299,"title":"","content":"In my 2015 VtM, the Antediluvians are bound for ten thousand years, each guarded by an ancient order of ghouls trained to perverse their eternal sleep. The ghouls are provided artificial Vitae through ancient relics that transform animal blood into the blood of 4th generation vampires, though the artificial Vitae may not be used to create blood bonds or new vampires. Each order obeys a six thousand year old 4th generation vampire, each a child of the trapped Antediluvian that they guard, though Tremere is trapped by a 4th generation child of Saulot and Giovanni is trapped by a 4th generation child of Cappadocius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:25:22-07:00","id":939328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939293#post939293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't use the Antedeluvians as active components in my chronicles. I only use them for historical event explanation, and to lay out a very general idea of the Jyhad so it provides structure to the politics and events happening in the setting.<br /> <br /> The antedeluvians were in torpor for much of recorded history. I had Cappadocius as the most active (since his actions are just too important to the backstory of the Cappadocians and therefore the Giovanni). In order to make any future Gehenna truly terrifying, I had his three partial awakenings from torpor all coincide with plague epidemics. I thought that it was appropriate the founder of the Clan of Death be associated (caused?) with mass death. I wanted to associate an antedeluvian rising with the idea of terrible calamities that would inaugur the end of the world. The first was during the Plague of Cyprian around AD 250 when the antedeluvian was converted to Christianity. The second was the Plague of Justinian around AD 541 when the Feast of Folly occurred. The last was during the Black Death. The association of Cappadocius' rising with great plagues that imperil humanity is one reason the Camarilla elders looked askance at the Giovanni purge of the rest of their clan mates.<br /> <br /> None of the other antedeluvians were active during the historical period. They've been in torpor or dead since before 3000 BC. Any rumors of their activity, particular with Set, is actually caused by one of their first childer, 4th generation methuselahs of extreme age and power. Prior to that, the antedeluvians were the old god-kings of the Mesopotamian city state legends although a few wandered off to other areas (Set, Ravnos, Saulot). (The Second City was Babel).<br /> <br /> There is a throw away line in the Vampire corebook that the Ventrue antedeluvian is known to be destroyed. That clan is the only one not manipulated by its antedeluvian, and therefore this is the main historical reason the clan is trusted enough to be the traditional leaders among the vampires. I push this heavily. Neonates don't care or don't believe, but I have the NPC elders make cryptic references to that every now and again so the PCs know this is what all or most of the elders actually believe.<br /> <br /> The historical destruction/diablerie of several antedeluvians during the Middle Ages are all essentially faked no matter how successful they seemed to be.<br /> <br /> For the structure of the Jyhad, I had to determine which were truly destroyed and which weren't. Then I had to figure out what each of the survivors wanted in broad terms, and how the setting backstory worked with it. Although I must admit I have not given it much though. I have no details only broad outlines. Usually, it's not important at all. However, if some PC really wanted to investigate the Jyhad, I have at least an idea of where to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice description, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>.<br /> <br /> I actually make Gehenna a myth which the Antedeluvians have lived in spite of. The prophecy of Gehenna when the Antedeluvians will arise and devour vampiredom dates back to the Second City and Malkav in my games. This despite the fact the Antedeluvians were frequently ruling alongside their progeny as late as the 14th century (with Cappadocius being the last to fall asleep with the Giovanni).<br /> <br /> The Antedeluvians when they arose generally handled matters like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Antedeluvians rise.<br /> 2. Antedeluvians summons all of their clan<br /> 3. The Antedeluvian eats the ones they hate and spares the one they don't, often feeding them blood to lower their generations.<br /> <br /> (So basically like the Feast of Folly but Cappadocius didn't reclaim his blood)<br /> <br /> The idea they would some day lose control and devour ALL of their children, leaving a nightmarish wasteland is as much the Antedeluvians nightmare as it is their progeny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-09-2019, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:49:04-07:00","id":939338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level#post938911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How powerful are yours?</div> </div> </div> </div>Infinity blood pool, infinity blood points per turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What can they do? </div> </div> </div>Plot device level disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What CAN'T they do? </div> </div> </div>Become mortal, pass as mortal, interact with mortal society in any way other than &quot;YOU CATTLE!!!&quot;, interfere into the higher-level plotlines of other supernaturals (e.g. destroy the Technocracy),<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what does it take to kill one? </div> </div> </div>For most, a direct hit with nuke will do. For some, such as Tzimisce/the Eldest and Earth-melded Ennoia, only things like a full gamma-frying of Earth from space by the Technocracy will work.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12156-the-caitiff-antediluvian","name":"The Caitiff Antediluvian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T03:07:46-07:00","id":939419,"title":"","content":"I've never used them, but if I did they'd essentially be plot-based. Basically slightly weaker Caine stats (but even Infinity -1 for stats is pretty spiffy) with a correspondingly broad or narrow impact on the plot as necessary. If I'm playing up the Jihad angle, they probably don't show up at all but you can infer that you're <i>somehow</i> doing <i>something's</i> bidding. Since they predate every civilization on the globe, they've learned how to be extremely subtle, except in plot-related cases where someone finds one that's been sleeping under the desert for a couple thousand years and they accidentally woke them up enough to psychically broadcast creepy lovecraftian nonsense that the plot revolves around. If I'm not playing up the Jihad angle, I'd be hard pressed to think of many examples that would make bringing in something with that kind of power make sense for the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T03:22:33-07:00","id":939425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level#post938911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How powerful are yours?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Antedeluvian, not all are created equal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What can they do? </div> </div> </div>Neat thematic and fundimentally physical things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What CAN'T they do? </div> </div> </div>Manipulate the other realms with ease. With raw power they can can bend things by accident(the illusions of Chimestry for example bending the dreaming by result but Ravana could not say shape the dreaming directly). But kindred are things of the physical world that's why they all seem to get bored and try to become something else. Once you are not Kindred like say being a mass of Shadows or the Madness Network you are by nature not an Antedeluvian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what does it take to kill one? </div> </div> </div>Filling in all their health levels with Agg? I mean they aren't spirits so you don't need to have a &quot;right way&quot; to kill them. Of course killing them might be all part of their &quot;Become more powerful than you can possibly imagine!&quot; plan to stop being kindred. <br /> <br /> <br /> A better answer might be &quot;How do you thwart his/her/its plans?&quot; But that's really a case by case issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:18:55-07:00","id":939509,"title":"","content":"One thing that I would like to implement if I ever run a chronicle involving the clan founders, would be the fact that just as an Ante's power is almost god-like, their original curses/weakness given by Caine are equally strong and crippling. This means that the clan weaknesses we know are much more severe or magnified, and in some cases near fatal to the Antes. Let me explain and give you some examples:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Tzimisce: The soil dependency of the Tzimisce affects the founder much severely in the sense that he doesn't just need a handful of his ancestral's home soil, but massive quantities of it, if he ever rests in foreign soil he starts losing his vampiric powers until he's driven to torpor. Obviously, the Eldest is practically immortal when in his home land, but if he was ever buried in foreign ground it would almost immediately incapacitate him, needless to say that if he was ever 'killed' while resting or trapped in foreign soil, it would be enough to destroy him entirely.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Ventrue: Just as the Ventrue can only drink from their particular blood type, the original curse would manifest on the Ventrue Ante as not just an incredibly specific and narrow feeding preference, but as an allergy to any other type of blood, an allergy that makes any other blood pure poison to the Ante and could potentially destroy him entirely, or leave him completely incapacitated for a final coup de grace.<br /> <br /> Obviously some of the other clan weaknesses would require a bit more tampering, but ideally they should all have the potential to be used against the Antes in some way, and possibly being the only way to truly destroy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Please check out my artwork for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/158767-i-bring-exalted-artwork-portraits-sketches\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/648775-vampire-character-artwork\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Masquerade</a> and at my <a href=\"http://lord-leafar.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DeviantArt page</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3202-lord-leafar","name":"Lord-Leafar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:16:25-07:00","id":939543,"title":"","content":"Powerful enough that they can motivate vast meta-plots.<br /> <br /> Weak enough that somehow we know the names of all the Antedeluvians whose clans have Obfuscate: Haqim, Malkav, Sutekh and Absimilliard.<br /> <br /> I would expect Obfuscate 10 would make everyone assume your clan is a bloodline. &quot;Oh, the Baali? They don't haaaave and antedeluvian.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:32:39-07:00","id":939709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939543#post939543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powerful enough that they can motivate vast meta-plots.<br /> <br /> Weak enough that somehow we know the names of all the Antedeluvians whose clans have Obfuscate: Haqim, Malkav, Sutekh and Absimilliard.<br /> <br /> I would expect Obfuscate 10 would make everyone assume your clan is a bloodline. &quot;Oh, the Baali? They don't haaaave and antedeluvian.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Memory%27s_Fading_Glimpse\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Memory%27s_Fading_Glimpse\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Memory%27s_Fading_Glimpse\" target=\"_blank\"> http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Memory%27s_Fading_Glimpse </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:18:30-07:00","id":939782,"title":"","content":"I've never used them when I've run games, but I like the depictions of them as basically inhuman forces of nature in the &quot;Crucible of God&quot; Gehenna scenario. They're so old and powerful that they're on the cusp of abandoning normal physical forms entirely and becoming something like gods. (Set actually <i>is</i> a god, albeit an ancient one with very few modern worshipers.) Their inherent powers over their own descendants can be used on a planetwide scale, as can the clan disciplines they've developed to the tenth dot.<br /> <br /> The 3rd generation vampires that date back to the Middle Ages are more human scale. They're more or less equivalent to some of the Bronze Age methuselahs, with maybe more focus on their special fields of study and less on generalized powers and skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:22:48-07:00","id":939784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level#post938911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How powerful are yours?<br /> <br /> What can they do?<br /> <br /> What CAN'T they do?<br /> <br /> And what does it take to kill one?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned it takes story and plot to limit and destroy my Antediluvians as well, but I don't play them as all-powerful and their great intellects are in my setting greatly scarred by extensive madness and delusions, which of course means that in my personal fanon, I've axed a fair few of the Ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:06:48-07:00","id":939806,"title":"","content":"I just want to throw in a thought: even the antes were young once. I'm on the side that everything in the world is working along the same game-rules, so in my book they always had the benefits of being 3rd generation, but they also were neonates and ancilae for a time with closer to human stats and low disciplines (3rd gen doens't automaticly mean 9+ stats from the start for me...), so in the beginning probably they and their progeny had an easier time destroying and diablerizing them and the major 13+ were the cunning enough to outlive their peers or the childer of their less-cunning ones. After that, along the thousands of years they were growed insanely powerful, but their surviving methuselah children also, so not an unbridgeable a power gap between them and older antes are more powerful than younger ones (although they might sleeping for a long time and younger ones might be more active and even among the original antes some of them might be more active than others, so again, the power lever could be varied).<br /> <br /> Another bit worth considering that the antes were active in days when the technological level was infinitely lower. Sure, among the first settlements of humankind they seemed as gods and ruled as such. Now? They'd have a lot harder time. That's one of the reasons why I think their awakening wouldn't mean the end of the world, but more that they'd try to wrestle the control from (or of) the sects and the methuselash and turn the shadow war against each other to 11. Sure they'd snack a lot of neonates and ancilla after awakening for breakfast and later along the way and those are the reasons why everybody are frightened of them and...<br /> <br /> ...people always construct myths and apocalypse tales. Much younger religions than the antes themselves have them and people &quot;see the signs&quot; every-fucking-time. I don't know why vampires'd be different. It's also in the methuselash's interest to spread these tales to undermine the workings of their biggest rivals. I think most of the vampire origin story is just that: a story which has bits of truth but warped and mystified along the ages.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea that the antes don't really want to rise and rule, or eat everyone. Maybe the ones whom didn't go to torpor willingly, they probably plot revenge, but lot of them just had enough of the world and bored themselves to sleep or trying to be something more than vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T20:29:42-07:00","id":939933,"title":"","content":"Antedilivian power level?<br /> <br /> Like &quot;he watches anime and never kissed a girl&quot; power level or...?<br /> <br /> Just kidding. Sorry, I had to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light inspires illusion and interpretation. Truth can only be found in darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3971-12dollarburrito","name":"12dollarburrito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T20:31:56-07:00","id":939934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>12dollarburrito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939933#post939933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antedilivian power level?<br /> <br /> Like &quot;he watches anime and never kissed a girl&quot; power level or...?<br /> <br /> Just kidding. Sorry, I had to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is funny because I met my wife at an anime convention.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:37:54-07:00","id":941618,"title":"","content":"For something more useful then the power of plot, which has been stated so often it is essentially useless someone could give any example what so ever of a Antediluvian that they had using the power of plot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay for something more useful, I have the Antediluvians essentially very mighty, but essentially weaker then Incarna spirits until they transcend their human form, and then they essentially start becoming more like a spirit. But Antediluvians I have them like the mightiest Methuselahs, like Baba Yaga, Ur-Shulgi, Japheth, ect. But they have access to Disciplines at the Tenth Level, and have a bit more exp. Why a lot of the Mightiest Methesulahs are beefy is because they could play around and invent 8-9 level disciplines, and combo disciplines, and Rituals. Antes I don't like having all 9/10s, but they do have high stats and some stats maxed. I imagine each Ante has most disciplines they aren't interested in at 5, some at zero for instance like say if say Veddartha doesn't want any Tzimice taint from Vicissitude. Their clan Disciplines at 10, and maybe a few more at ten, particularly if a bloodline has them, like giving Set Potence 10.<br /> <br /> I have it reaching the tenth level of a discipline makes it easier for an ante to develop lower level powers, essentially allowing them to learn powers at the cost of the level. The Antes I have are essentially using Caitiffs no favored disciplines rule. But like other Ancient level disciplines level Ten can be learned multiple times, but is always expensive. You can track a lot of an Antes history by each time they learn an Alternate level 10 discipline for instance, Lasombra gave up his human form by learning Obtenebration 10 a 2nd time transforming him into a true creature of the Abyss, perhaps one more bump up and it transcends vampirism and becomes essentially a spirit/alien.<br /> <br /> This allows me to say some Antes are better at things then others that also mastered it. Like say Lasombra mastered Potence to the Tenth level, but it only learned it once, but what if Brujah/Troile/Ilyes learned it twice essentially representing a more thorough and diversified super strength. So Maybe it would take Lasombra a night to shatter a mountain, but Brujah could shatter one in a scene, or if expending great resources maybe shattering it in an instance.<br /> <br /> I have it the Antediluvians that survived each have combos/powers to protect them from curses, and control, each likely different and unique. And they have redundancies in place for sticky situations they are in danger, for instance Samael died slaying Tzimisce but the Eldest gestated in the Womb of his Childe, but things like this reincarnation are speedbumps that consume several centuries for the Ante in question. But Antediluvians can be overwhelmed by Methuselah level powers, particularly if caught in a weakened state, think Galactus getting whomped if trying to eat Earth when weakened by hunger. But if preparing Antes often have rituals or combo powers that can harm beings a step above them, like Set Cursing Tribes of Fera and Incarna.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ravnos was essentially going to loose to three beings one step below him in power, but he got jumped by a Conspiracy of Magical Scientists using Archmage effects/artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:39:31-07:00","id":941619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939543#post939543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powerful enough that they can motivate vast meta-plots.<br /> <br /> Weak enough that somehow we know the names of all the Antedeluvians whose clans have Obfuscate: Haqim, Malkav, Sutekh and Absimilliard.<br /> <br /> I would expect Obfuscate 10 would make everyone assume your clan is a bloodline. &quot;Oh, the Baali? They don't haaaave and antedeluvian.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We could know those specific names because of Obfuscate 10, hiding their real names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T14:53:15-07:00","id":942247,"title":"","content":"I suspect it's not so much weakness as ego that results in the antediluvians with Obfuscate as a clan discipline being known, hence Haquim and Set's clans basically also being cults that worship them as gods. They may have used their powers to hide things other than their identities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:04:19-07:00","id":942254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=942247#post942247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it's not so much weakness as ego that results in the antediluvians with Obfuscate as a clan discipline being known, hence Haquim and Set's clans basically also being cults that worship them as gods. They may have used their powers to hide things other than their identities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> or Haquim isn't a warrior....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:37:02-07:00","id":942280,"title":"","content":"The newer stuff for the Assamites does say that Obfuscate really wasn't a thing for them in their early days, and only the Warriors had it natively as recently as Dark Ages stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:50:44-07:00","id":947768,"title":"","content":"My Antediluvians are vastly powerful and vastly limited. Being closer to the source of vampirism, they have more power, but the curses also have a much stronger grip on them, and are harder to blunt or shake. Sunlight comes down like a hammer, and despite their mastery of disciplines, there is no power or ritual that will let them soak it with stamina. They needed more kine blood to sustain themselves and fuel their powers when they were young, but now they (mostly) have advanced cases of Methuselah thirst, where only the 4th or 5th generations vitae will quench their thirst. Once again, powers and disciplines that Kindred further away from the source can use to lighten the vitae cost of disciplines and actions do not function for them. Fire burns hotter when it burns them. Those that still have physical forms have grown less human and more vampire in visage over time.<br /> <br /> Saulot sacrificed most of his clan and centuries of time, but is currently in control of a body that has not yet fully developed Methuselahs thirst, allowing an unprecedented freedom to act.<br /> <br /> Antediluvians are very different from each other though. Most seek to transcend their curses in some manner. Spiritually, biologically, or through magic. Most are on some path of enlightenment, although not all.<br /> <br /> They spend most of their time in torpor, making subtle moves with blood-cheap disciplines. Occasionally they wake, devour those of their childer and grandchilder too slow or dim to protect themselves, and make moves in the temporal world, then sink back into glutted torpor like fat ticks.<br /> <br /> I don't hold with the direct assumption that Antediluvians have 10 in the three disciplines of their clans. Most are less tied to clan disciplines than their descendants assume. Also, I don't hold level 10 disciplines to be part of the linear xp progression. Level 10s are mastery on an almost conceptual level, and a degree of magnitude greater than level 9. It generally takes millennia to master one. After 15 000 years, the antes average two each. Absimilliard, Tremere and Augustus Giovanni have no level 10s. The ones concentrating on spiritual transcendence and esoteric matter normally have more than the more temporally oriented ones.<br /> <br /> Antes do, however, have a monstrous number of dots in disciplines in general, and can be expected to have multiple level 8 and 9 powers in all the common disciplines.<br /> <br /> Also, I've assumed that despite the reputation of Caine as the source and inceptor of all disciplines, beating the original clan disciplines out of the metal of the Curse was not easy and took much longer than assumed. Many of the tales of the first and second city, with kindred fighting like cats in a sack, makes more sense if viewed through the perspective of Antediluvians being limited to the first agricultural civilizations as the only areas with the population density to sustain them, and initially lacking the disciplines to just go off to some remote corner of the world and feeding on nomads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:40:37-07:00","id":965008,"title":"","content":"As Methuselahs can manipulate and alter civilizations, Antediluvians can manipulate multiple civilizations simultaneously, guiding large swathes of humanity. However, at that scale, they're very likely to bump against the influence of mighty supernatural forces, and so they usually (Zapathasura says hi) play it cool and exercise guile and restraint with a subtle Jyhad or more introspective personal projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12326-slick-willy","name":"Slick Willy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:03:02-07:00","id":965211,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite character sheets comes from Legend of the Five Rings - specifically, from Way of the Dragon in the game's first edition. In that edition, they &quot;statted&quot; Togashi Yokuni, champion of the Dragon Clan.<br /> <br /> Togashi Yokuni was actually Togashi, the legendary founder of the clan, in a secret disguise as one champion of the clan or another for over a millennium at that point. Already a god when he descended in the beginning of civilization, Togashi had become terrifyingly powerful after 1100 years on Ningen-do, and in fact, his stat block basically can be summed up with the line &quot;Yokuni gets what Yokuni wants.&quot; Unless you are threatening him with an entity of similar power (i.e. an Elemental Dragon), you lose unless he doesn't want you to.<br /> <br /> And that's how I see Antediluvians. Unless you're playing Methuselah, you're not going to be in the range of power needed to threaten an Antediluvian directly. You're just not. They've all mastered their own Disciplines to a degree that you cannot fathom (even with just level 9 disciplines, you're doing things most vampires can't understand), and have likely mastered many others to a degree that is still beyond non-Elders' capability of achieving. Their mundane potential at tasks that don't involve modern knowledge (and in some cases, even those), before factoring in powers of the blood, can outpace a neonate or ancilla who isn't dedicated to the same task or using their powers to try to match.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, to threaten an Antediluvean, you need either significant planning or significant power (see the bit about Methuselahs), and likely both. Now, their plans you can potentially undermine - their plans are subtle and vast, but they still can be unbalanced or upset by someone with enough resources. But to actually fight an Antediluvean, especially one who's been active for a while rather than just sleeping, is insanity in these nights in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:09:51-07:00","id":965385,"title":"","content":"To me, the Antediluvians are gods, beyond any mortal's comprehension in power and they cannot be destroyed except by another godlike being. They are prophesied to arise and to openly rule over the earth until God's judgement. This being the case, I do not recognize the Week of Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:01:48-07:00","id":965411,"title":"","content":"Well, in the one game I've played where an Antediluvian bit the big one (at the hands of PC's)...<br /> <br /> It was a Mage: the Ascension game. My PC's (an entire cabal of Masters, plus their equally powerful allies, plus an Archmaster or two) channeled the entire force of a multiple-megaton, Prime-infused, Forces-buffered, <i>co-located</i>, spirit nuke through sympathetic magic straight to [Tzimisce]'s Pattern. That did the trick.<br /> <br /> Well, after fighting it on foot more than once, and it constantly coming right back for more. One of those fights saw the birth of a rote my players immediately started calling the &quot;Hammer of Dawn&quot; (Correspondence portal to the Sun, buffered and directed by Forces, and infused with Prime).<br /> <br /> It was also fighting Arikel and the entire (still-surviving members of the) Toreador clan, a literal army of garou, and the Technocracy at the same time, which distracted it long enough for the PC's to pull off the Correspondence nuke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:00:46-07:00","id":965440,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll make it very short because I'm quite busy right now...<br /> <br /> The thing I see with all this theory/concept of &quot;antedeluvians being absolutely invincible&quot; that became very strong in the third edition of vampire is that it creates many problems for the game. First of all, it shouldn't make much sense as in the history of cainites, the third generation vampires are known for having killed the second generation vampires, so, why are the 13 so special that they became invincible? Not to mention that it takes away one of the key concepts that shapes the mood in vampire games, that is the absolute uncertainty about the future, no one should have guaranteed power for all of eternity. Treason and paranoia and I think I shouldn't even need to mention: mystery, are key concepts in vampire, when you take part of these concepts away, by, for instance, implyng that every antedeluvian who were destroyed, wasn't really destroyed or that it was part os a scheme of their own etc... it kind of ruin everything in my opinion. That's part of the reason why the books of gehena were imo a very bad idea.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but english isn't my mother language, but I hope you have understood my point somehow.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:18:55-07:00","id":965496,"title":"","content":"One misconception that I'd like to add here is the meaning of &quot;time&quot; in cainites. The power of the cainites is in their blood, their essence, it's a metaphysical concept, it's not like a simple formulae like: &quot;oh you have 15.000 years of existence, so you should be able to master a discipline to level 10...&quot;hell no! Time is just one of the aspects of the vampiric existence and there are MANY rituals of all sorts that allow a cainite to absorb the powers and knoledges of another cainite (Blade of the Forbidden Flower, of the Tremere even allows you to place the essence of another cainite's abilities and disciplines into a weapon and there are many other similar powers...), and I'm not even mentioning the fabled Amaranth. With that being said, it's pretty obvious that if you would make a character sheet for an antedeluvian like Augustus Giovanni or Tremere (something imo completelly unnecessary...) you should give them a level 10 in their field of expertise (i.e: Thaumaturgy and Necromancy etc). This is so obvious that, with all due respect, it's hard for me to read somebody arguing that it shouldn't be the case when it's so obvious and you can even see it in the cannon etc...The World of Darkness isn't a linear and simplist world like that of D&amp;D etc (with all due respect for the players of these systems and worlds, as I'm only implying that they work with different aproaches to their respective realities). What has always attracted me, as an amateur philosopher myself, is this very aesthetic of WoD, I simply cannot understand why people argue over such irrelevant issues as &quot;what should the powers of a given cainite be etc...&quot;, it all depends on the World that the storyteller wants, it should fit their story and that's all. In short, nothing is &quot;simple&quot; in the WoD.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:24:17-07:00","id":965500,"title":"","content":"Your starting freebies/xp are not a function of your generation, so why would a 3rd generation automatically have a massively greater number of discipline dots than a 5th-4th generation of comparable time active (provided they both spent that time doing similarly edifying/difficult things)? Obviously the 5th gen cannot learn a level 10 discipline, but he would still have a commensurate number of lower level discipline dots or attributes or whatever. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:13:46-07:00","id":965936,"title":"","content":"First of all, the freebies/xp points given to a character are just guidelines (as MANY other things in the WoD), as a matter of fact one would expect someone to have acquired more knoledge if he or she had more time to do so (or at least the &quot;common sense&quot; see it this way...), but this is just a guideline, it's basically just one of many factors. People are different and so are cainites, there are average people and kindreds and gifted individuals who can do more with little time, so to speak. There are also genius who are able to come up with groundbreaking inventions/discoveries, like an Einstein, a Gutenberb, a Karl Benz etc and the same goes when one speak of cainites. So, with this in mind, every one is unique, it's not just math that defines what one should be able to do with a given time, again, as I mentioned, it's all subjective. Finally, getting to the point, cainites have their powers and even knoledges in their essence that is in their blood, and there are many ways to get this power/knoledge (i.e: Disciplines etc) by consuming the cainite's essence, be it through the well known act of amaranth/diablerie or through rituals that consume and therefore transfer all of the cainite essence to another cainite. So, there are a plethora of scenarios one could imagine where the Giovanni and the Tremere could have absorbed the essense and along with it the knowledge and power of countless cainites of the clans they came to persecute and destroy (capadocians and salubri).<br /> All in all, what I mean is that it's not so simplistic as the way some people are arguing here, it's all up to the Storyteller and the way he sees fit into his game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:10:47-07:00","id":966051,"title":"","content":"Well if they are called an Antediluvian then they are over 10k years old, and by then having a power one step above is a big deal. And in my take on Antes achieving mastery of a Discipline makes learning any alternate powers below 10 cost only the experience of the Level. So only 9 Experience to learn a methuselah power a childe invented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:21:02-07:00","id":966058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=966051#post966051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if they are called an Antediluvian then they are over 10k years old, and by then having a power one step above is a big deal. And in my take on Antes achieving mastery of a Discipline makes learning any alternate powers below 10 cost only the experience of the Level. So only 9 Experience to learn a methuselah power a childe invented.</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point aren't you just making up house rules to inflate their already immense power? It's not like after being around for 10k years they shouldn't have XP to spare.<br /> In the end I don't think it ends up mattering anyways since the overall effect is to give them access to whatever powers you as a ST feel like anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:45:19-07:00","id":966070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=966058#post966058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At that point aren't you just making up house rules to inflate their already immense power? It's not like after being around for 10k years they shouldn't have XP to spare.<br /> In the end I don't think it ends up mattering anyways since the overall effect is to give them access to whatever powers you as a ST feel like anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if we go by that logic nothing matters anyways, its all up to the ST. I'm just saying I don't like Antes to be omnipotent, but I find my houserule sensible for them being Mighty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:18:38-07:00","id":966095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=939215#post939215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome ideas <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> <b>Set</b> died at the hands of werewolves. It's an ignominous but very true end for the one Cainite who thought he was a God.<br /> <br /> <b>Osiris</b> the 14th Antedeluvian was either embraced by Irad or Set himself. Dead at Set's hands.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b> is dead at Troile's hands. He was actually kind of a shit leader too and everything we attribute to Ventrue as a clan comes from Mithras and Tiamat.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> is dead-dead. Nuking from orbit was the only way to be sure. The sunlight just finished the job. However, it's an in-universe debate Hazmiel was killed instead since the difference between the two would be negligible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Set, with Serpentis 10, fled into Duat in my games. His body destroyed, he waits patiently for his Clan to resurrect him. When they succeed, months before Gehenna, he summons most of them (PCs and non Set Worshippers feel the Summons but don't go) and devours them.<br /> <br /> Osiris is about, but horribly weak and infertile. Set did kill him, but his wife resurrected him.<br /> <br /> Ventru; Dominate 3 is a thing. Fortitude 10 is also a thing. I'm sure Troile believes that she killed him.<br /> <br /> Ravana; Chimerstry 10 anyone? All that is confirmed is that something that looked like the Ravnos antediluvian was killed after a ridiculous amount of punishment. Master of illusions; it isn't a big leap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T02:26:11-07:00","id":966117,"title":"","content":"As hackneyed as it may seem, it really does depend on the story, but in general here's what I thought about the Antediluvians in my games.<br /> <br /> Antediluvian can mean a few different things in my games based on the character discussing it<ul><li>A Third Generation Cainite</li> <li>A Cainite who survived the flood that destroyed the First City</li> <li>A Third Generation Cainite who survived the flood that destroyed the First City</li> </ul><br /> [A note on numbers, all of these assume a game set in modern (2016) times]<br /> <br /> Abilities: Assume they have high to max ranks in Abilities that make sense in association with their mindset and powers; other Abilities can vary wildly (when in doubt I err on the side of slightly higher than lower as most of these Cainites are immensely old and powerful). The exception are modern Abilities such as Firearms and Technology; access to these is dependent on the Cainite in question being active in the modern era for a reasonable amount of time to have learned such new Abilities.<br /> <br /> True Antediluvian: A Third Generation Cainite who survived the flood that destroyed the First City (the date of the flood varies, but I generally place it around 10k years ago). The number in my games is not always 13, I've had some games where others have survived but lay in torpor, or listened to Caine's rules and did not embrace.<ul><li>They have reached level 10 in their clan disciplines and possibly one or two others. The power of a level 10 discipline depends on the needs of the game, anywhere from somewhat more powerful than level 9 to rivaling the archspheres of awakened magick, regardless a level 10 is a way to counter another level 10 (forcing an opposed roll).</li> <li>They have level 5+ in all the other common disciplines (Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Potence, Presence)</li> <li>They know at least one (likely 2 or 3) 'obscure' disciplines (between level 1-7)</li> <li>At least one Attribute at 10, other primary Attributes at 8 to 10, others at 5+ (barring a 0 from a clan weakness)</li> <li>Often have Methuselah's Thirst or some other restrictions on what they can derive sustenance from</li> <li>Some may have transcended Cainite flesh and become something else, some possible examples<ul><li>[Lasombra] becoming a shadow being of the Abyss</li> <li>[Tzimisce] suffusing Vicissitude and able to reform/control (imagine the Agents taking over someone in the Matrix) anyone with the discipline</li> <li>[Malkav] become a psychic entity within or the Malkavian Madness Network itself</li> <li>[Gangrel] becoming one with the Earth through Protean</li> </ul></li> <li>Destroying such creatures is possible but supremely difficult, some examples of what one might need to do so<ul><li>Caine</li> <li>A Second Generation Cainite of appropriate age</li> <li>The assistance of the True Antediluvian itself (example Cappadocius and Augustus Giovanni)</li> <li>Another True Antediluvian</li> <li>An Archmage with Archspheres</li> <li>A Kuei-jin Arhat (Dharma level 10, assuming such entities can interact with our world)</li> <li>Multiple (at least 5) Methuselahs (Fourth Generation) of great age (over a thousand years) or another supernatural with equivalent power and age, some examples Archmages (Arete 6+ without Archspheres), Rank 6 Garou/Fera, Bodhisattvas (Dharma 9). Some will likely die in the attempt.</li> <li>Many (10+) Methuselahs (Fifth and Sixth Generation) of great age or another supernatural with equivalent power and age, some examples Master Mages (Arete 5, 3+ Spheres at 5), Rank 5 Garou/Fera, Ancestors (Dharma 7 and 8). Most will likely die in the attempt.</li> <li>Lesser being might be able to destroy such a creature, but it would require catastrophic casualties (thousands or millions in the case of normal humans) and a great deal of luck or massive destuction (for example multiple successful nuclear strikes might kill such a creature).</li> <li>Even if 'successful' the True Antediluvian might survive in some way, such as Saulot within Tremere's body or [Lasombra] if he entered the Abyss</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> False Antediluvian: A Third Generation Cainite who is younger than the flood that destroyed the First City often attaining that power from diablerie. Canonically this could be Tremere, Augustus Giovanni, Gratiano de Veronese, Lugoj Blood-Breaker, and possibly Troile depending when you place the diablerie of [Brujah]/Ilyes). Numbers can vary wildly based on how long ago they were embraced and how active they were after they achieved Third Generation, the numbers below reflect the rough power level I place the canonical False Antediluvians.<ul><li>They have reached level 10 in one of their clan disciplines (if possible depending on plot, a False Antediluvian may have believed they consumed a Third Generation, but may not actually succeeded or have been partially stopped by the machinations of their meal).</li> <li>They have reached level 6+ in their other clan disciplines</li> <li>Generally have some knowledge of 3+ common disciplines (between level 1-5) and one at level 6+</li> <li>Generally have one Attribute at 10, other primary Attributes at 6+, others vary along 'normal' lines</li> <li>Likely can no longer feed on animals, Methuselah's Thirst is also possible</li> <li>Destroying such a creature is easier than a True Antediluvian as they are much younger, so assume everything as per True Antediluvians will work (and more easily) and lesser beings stand a much greater chance of success with lower (but still high) casualties. Indeed depending on their age a single ancient Methuselah could be a threat to a False Antediluvian.</li> </ul><br /> Flood Methuselahs: In some games I've had Cainites of Fourth Generation also survive the flood that destroyed the First City, and could technically be called Antediluvians because of that.<ul><li>They have reached level 9 in their clan disciplines</li> <li>They all have level 6+ in Fortitude or some other way to explain how they survived the flood (examples A high level Blood Magic ritual, or a high level Protean power)</li> <li>They have level 5+ in all the common disciplines</li> <li>They likely know at least one 'obscure' discipline (between level 1-5)</li> <li>One Attribute at 9, other primary Attributes at 7 or 8, others at 5+ (again barring clan weaknesses)</li> <li>Methuselah's Thirst is common, and inability to feed on animals is the norm</li> <li>Three such creatures could be a threat to a True Antediluvian (although at least one will die in the attempt) and a single Flood Methuselah is a threat to a False Antediluvian</li> <li>A Flood Methuselah is likely to be as hard to destroy as a False Antediluvian if not moreso considering they had the resilience to survive the flood</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:28:22-07:00","id":967805,"title":"","content":"As a person who primarily does Technocracy games:<br /> <br /> Antediluvians are Class GODLIKEs, they're stupidly powerful, ridiculously versatile and nigh-invulnerable to even Technocratic light and medium weapons. This means that they casually laugh at having pistols that shoot with the force of an RPG explode in their face, and respond to a strike team of HITMarks by ripping them apart and using their arms as slashing weapons. Generally on the side of powers, their abilities are huge and destructive, impacting the scene when they are invoked and honestly resemble Utterances from Mummy or the more powerful Charms from Exalted more than vampiric powers.<br /> <br /> There has been two scenes in my games where Antediluvians have been relevant, and both have made my players very afraid.<br /> <br /> The first was of course the Week of Nightmares where they were &quot;lucky&quot; enough to play characters at ground zero while Ravana was doing stuff like recreate biblical desires with illusions and using perfect defenses such as &quot;nuh uh i was never there at all&quot; or &quot;no ur the one hit&quot; or &quot;faq u targeting systems are a lie&quot;. He also did stuff like spontaneously make new animal races whenever he felt like it to bolster his Animalism, and a lot of the fallout from that game has been containment teams trying to figure out what to do with all the new deadly wildlife made of solid murder that an ancient dead monster felt he needed for his defense.<br /> <br /> (This one was actually an interesting case since neither me, nor my players expected them to survive and indeed had the expectation of dying heroically to halt the ancient monster, but what did happen was that due to clever tactics and thinking on their part, they managed to harry it like wolves, keeping up the pressure and in <i>some way</i> still succeed their rolls all the time until the heavy ordnance arrived to cover them and an Aurora could extract them. They were named Heroes of The Technocracy for the vital information on it's defenses and were promoted to higher ranks each, only two of those characters are still alive, one having a place on the Void Engineer Admiralty while the other is an NWO Director. They both miss their Amalgam very much and the Director is a broken woman who barely pulls herself through every day, and keeps a picture of her love that died a few weeks later from having his mind broken by the many hazards from the Antediluvian's mental attacks.)<br /> <br /> The second one was in 2012, being a battle against Toreador. Toreador took the form of an androgynous figure of absolute beauty and was classified as a high-class memetic hazard, requiring that all agents who volunteered for the mission undergo invasive surgery to protect them from looking at it and getting caught worshipping it. Toreador moved with such speed that it simply walked through the battlefield, and when it actually ran, the shockwave knocked helicopters out of the air and liquidized any nearby agents. It possessed a radiant aura that made it reminiscent of a god incarnate and it simply saw through any plans and disguises. It was also fully awake and managed to wreak havoc on five cities simply by existing nearby before it was stopped with a casualty rate 87.6% among the Technocratic agents sent against it.<br /> <br /> I generally establish a dichotomy between the young/high-Generation vampires that my players can scythe through effortlessly with their Technocratic hardware, and the old/low-Generation vampires that are extreme threats and tend to pull some bullshit out of their ass whenever they are actually threatened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:47:07-07:00","id":974172,"title":"","content":"I've always hated the &quot;They don't have stats, they are plot devices&quot; sort of logic. It's the sign of a weak GM in my opinion.<br /> I don't have any problem giving an Antediluvian 50 points in disciplines, and calling them good. In my games Baba Yaga is more powerful than many, if not most, of the Antediluvians.<br /> Vasilisa is probably the dumbest character white wolf ever wrote up, with her &quot;transcending disciplines&quot; bullshit. <br /> Having said all that, I'd really play up the advantages that they did have. They'd be masters of their powers and disciplines, and I'd let them use every dirty trick in the book...<br /> But I don't see any reason why they have to be unstoppable gods to have an interesting story. If you can't figure out a way to take over an entire continent with a single Anti, then you just aren't being creative enough.<br /> Puppet Master? Dream World? Pulse of the Canaille? Army of Beasts?<br /> Why do you need more than these?<br /> Any one of those abilities makes you a god. And an Antediluvian has two or three of them. <br /> Having said that, I don't see any reason that they have to be undefeatable. Even by much weaker characters.<br /> A single direct hit from a tank shell would toast almost any of the Antediluvians. Welcome to the modern world, bitches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12215-godslayer","name":"Godslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T01:28:00-07:00","id":974292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974172#post974172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any problem giving an Antediluvian 50 points in disciplines, and calling them good. In my games Baba Yaga is more powerful than many, if not most, of the Antediluvians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes no sense, both rules-wise and plot-wise.<br /> Baba Yaga is nowhere near an Antediluvian,to fight Nosferatu she had to summon six amazingly powerful Dragons, plus one of the Wyrm's Talons,Koshchey the deathless.<br /> Antediluvian are on Incarna or Oracles level of power, no methuselah can beat them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vasilisa is probably the dumbest character white wolf ever wrote up, with her &quot;transcending disciplines&quot; bullshit. </div> </div> </div>Why? It's really not unheard of: the favorite childes of the Ante's have always transcended their status as Methuselah, look at Japheth with his unique powers, or Ur-Shulgi as the herald of Haqim.<br /> <br /> The elder blood commands the younger one, it can shape it, remember that the whole evolution of the disciplines have been determined by the elders of the clans, so if the Antediluvian decides that some of his childrens need special powers he just makes so by commanding the blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't see any reason why they have to be unstoppable gods to have an interesting story. </div> </div> </div>Because is one of the main point of the Vampire lore?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Puppet Master? Dream World? Pulse of the Canaille? Army of Beasts?<br /> Why do you need more than these?<br /> Any one of those abilities makes you a god. And an Antediluvian has two or three of them. </div> </div> </div>Again you are forgetting the nature of the disciplines, no Antedeluvian has a single variant of power at level 10, he can have as many variants as he needs, just because he commands the blood.<br /> Even lessere elder vampires can &quot;shape&quot; the disciplines to their liking and needs, that's the reason there are so many variants of the same level for the elder discipline, because as I said the elder blood can &quot;shape&quot; the disciplines tu suit a specific need, and the blood of an Antediluvian can just master it to suit every needs on the fly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A single direct hit from a tank shell would toast almost any of the Antediluvians. Welcome to the modern world, bitches. </div> </div> </div>Lol, Ravnos withstood four nuclear strikes, a tank shell would bother and Antediluvian just like a fly could bother an elephant.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T03:09:09-07:00","id":974315,"title":"","content":"Antediluvians are powerful to the point where it becomes irrelevant. You think you can take on Haqim? Sure, but he just used a mix of Obfuscate 10 and Quietus 9 to remove the 6th Generation vampire from reality, alongside every single of his descendants, including you.<br /> <br /> Think you can take on Augustus Giovanni? He just raised you from the undead and you are now his slave.<br /> <br /> Troile? Nope, he just clotheslined your head off at Mach 20.<br /> <br /> Lasombra? Congratulations, you won yourself a one-way trip to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> It just does not matter what you can do at such levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:07:56-07:00","id":974390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974292#post974292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which makes no sense, both rules-wise and plot-wise.<br /> Baba Yaga is nowhere near an Antediluvian,to fight Nosferatu she had to summon six amazingly powerful Dragons, plus one of the Wyrm's Talons,Koshchey the deathless.<br /> Antediluvian are on Incarna or Oracles level of power, no methuselah can beat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did that mostly by hiding. One gets the impression that in an actual fight, if he can't avoid it, he would experience Final Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Lol, Ravnos withstood four nuclear strikes </div> </div> </div>No, he didn't. He was around four devices that were on par with nukes, but only affected spirits. As vampires are not spirits and have little, if any, connection to them, he wouldn't have been affected as a matter of course, but then again, neither would have a 15th gen neonate.<br /> <br /> Tank shells probably don't hurt them that much, though, that's true. But an actual nuclear weapon, particularly of a strategic yield? The flash alone could probably do it in on a direct hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:50:47-07:00","id":974435,"title":"","content":"No, the four nukes destroyed everything else that Ravnos had been fighting, (Wraiths, Werewolves, Mages, Kuei-Jin, something like 10,000 mortals, other), but he survived them, close to if not at ground zero. So clearly they where not just spirit only nukes. It's also within reason to assume that they might have been magically enhanced nukes, too, but regardless, they had the full affect on both the Antediluvian and everyone else in the area, and he survived all of them directly.<br /> <br /> It's also somewhat implied that the only reason that the sun finally killed him was that it was amplified incredibly heavily (x4 I believe), and even that wasn't instant.<br /> <br /> As for how I use them, well, I really don't. I think I've only used two, Giovanni and Tremere, who where both significantly less powerful than a &quot;true&quot; Antediluvian (either in the sense of being a 3rd Gen or in the sense of being an actual survivor of the great flood, regardless of Gen). Antediluvian's power levels, outside of being plot points, are very nearly god-like. Beyond the scope of even Mages in many ways, (an Antediluvian will overpower any mastery over Spheres in most cases on a one for one basis), except that Disciplines, Generation, and the like DO all have specific parameters. That is to say, that they do not work like Awakened Magic and allow them to create effects on a whim, though at their level of mastery, it might appear so or be close enough to be indistinguishable in some cases.<br /> <br /> They are still affected by the sun just like every other vampire, though likely have very high levels of Fortitude. Decapitation, with possible exceptions like Tzimisce will still kill them outright, and a stake through the heart will still put them down. They still need blood in order to function and remain outside of Torpor, however, I can also see them, (at least the original ones) having a degree of mystical control over their descendants less related to their Generation and more related to a side effect of Caine's cursing of them that passed onto their Clan.<br /> <br /> They still need/use/are restricted to all the rules involving Path Ratings, Virtues, Frenzy, etc. . ., very, very likely have multiple Traits at 10 or close, but not all, or even most. It's also very likely that they have basically seen and done almost everything, so probably not going to fall for 95% of any traps, tricks, or tactics that even a coterie of Elders come up with after a century of focused planning, and while technology might give an edge, it's just as much a burden when used against creatures that might have needed to do everything before the invention of the proverbial wheel or who do not see literally walking across the bottom of the ocean to get from one place to another as an obstacle. Basically, a flamethrower, moltov, or nuke just isn't enough. That's a first step in the 100+ point plan, not the finale. That's the sort of stuff that MIGHT work on a Methuselah. MIGHT.<br /> <br /> If the Antediluvians are active, either directly or through proxy, really just depends on the game at the time, although I begun to drift away from the style of having them and similarly old Cainties be too active while in Torpor, just because they have got to be extremely bored, and probably go into Torpor on purpose to get away from the world for a few centuries at a time and shake things up. Likewise, I tend to gravitate away from them being completely inhuman monsters that have one (or even a few) fanatical schemes above all else or completely unaware of technology or advancement. While they probably haven't mastered it, I would think that at least a cursory understanding of things that they might find marvelous, if not magical would be exactly the sort of thing that they would seek out to fight off the never ending boredom that is their only real foe, and &quot;micromanagement&quot; (even of States/countries/continents) has grown pointless to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:58:14-07:00","id":974481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974390#post974390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He did that mostly by hiding. One gets the impression that in an actual fight, if he can't avoid it, he would experience Final Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I doubt that a being who can use Potence 10 to throw mountains at you like if they were rocks (and make them invisibles with Obfuscate 10, remember the invisible missiles in TC 4?) or summon every animals of the earth to aid him and transmute them in the Colverfield monster would experience Final Death against anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, he didn't. He was around four devices that were on par with nukes, but only affected spirits. As vampires are not spirits and have little, if any, connection to them, he wouldn't have been affected as a matter of course, but then again, neither would have a 15th gen neonate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tank shells probably don't hurt them that much, though, that's true. But an actual nuclear weapon, particularly of a strategic yield? The flash alone could probably do it in on a direct hit. </div> </div> </div>No, I think you don't clearly remember the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> He was hit by spiritual nukes that affected <b>both </b>spirits and normal humans, in fact almost 60k peoples in bangladesh have been killed by the nukes.<br /> <br /> Page 123 Times of Thin Blood<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The typhoon caused an estimated 115,600 deaths by purely natural means as it flooded Bangladesh. As they were designed to do,<b> the bomb airburst caused serious property damage and death only in the immediate vicinity of the blast</b>, while still slaughtering the supernatural creatures many kilometeres distant. Only <b>60.800 Bangladeshis had died from the explosions and radiation.</b> </div> </div> </div>Page 126<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the sorcerers brought their most powerful weapons into the hellstorm: neutron bombs, built to project a radiation lethal to supernatural beings. They worked. The bombs destroyed all the supernatural creatures except the antideluvian itself -<b> but the bombs</b> and a day and night of battle with the Bodhisattvas<b> had weakened the Anceint</b> enough that, when the storm clouds parted, the reflected sunlight destroyed the ancient Cainite </div> </div> </div>The damages of the spirit nukes is explained in Ascension page 211.<br /> <br /> <br /> A spiritual nuke works as a neutron bombs, so it does 10 levels of aggravated damages in a radius of 140 meters, plus 10 dice of aggravated damages in the range of 350 meters, plus 10 dice of bashing damages in 1400 meters radius, plus 16 agg dice of radiations<br /> <br /> And he was hit by four of them, for a total of 40 levels of agg damages +40 dices of agg from the firestorm+ 40 dice of bashing + 64 dice of agg from the radiations.<br /> <br /> <br /> And he had fought for a day and a night with three incredibly powerful Bodhisattva (two of them were virtual Arhat in terms of powers) an horde of wraiths, and he was fighting during the day, with all the penalities it brings.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah obviously this is assuming the bombs were the &quot;average&quot; netruon bombs.<br /> If they weren't, the above mentioned damages would have been even greater (up to 30 levels agg,30 dices agg,30 bashind dice, and the same 16 radiation damages).<br /> <br /> <br /> So no, no nuclear strike can kill an Antediluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:04:47-07:00","id":974484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974435#post974435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also somewhat implied that the only reason that the sun finally killed him was that it was amplified incredibly heavily (x4 I believe), and even that wasn't instant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, x4.<br /> And that would mean 12 agg dice (soak 10 with fortitude) per turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a stake through the heart will still put them down. </div> </div> </div>TC 4 hints that this may not be the case: Saulot/Tremere's body was staked in the underground Tremere's chamber in Vienna after Tremere entered Etrius' body; when he returned after the Mexico City trip the stake (inscribed with runes, so probably a magical one) was on the ground, and Saulot was gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:45:50-07:00","id":974522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974481#post974481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no, no nuclear strike can kill an Antideluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this last statement. I think a Nuclear strike will kill any of the Antideluvians that aren't masters of Fotitude or have some other hand wavy power to survive (Vissicitude 10 comes to mind). Even the Fotitude 10 Antes are only surviving because of TT-version Aegis powers. They can't actually soak that amount of damage, they just get to magically survive it <i>because plot</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974484#post974484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, x4.<br /> And that would mean 12 agg dice (soak 10 with fortitude) per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers really don't matter. Like, not even a little bit. And I think it would be 12 levels, not dice. But even then, is it that the damage was multiplied or that there were 4 suns? 4 Suns would be a lot easier to soak, since they would be soaked individually. But again, this stuff happened the way it did because the writers wrote it that way, not because any sort of dice rolling would support it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974484#post974484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TC 4 hints that this may not be the case: Saulot/Tremere's body was staked in the underground Tremere's chamber in Vienna after Tremere entered Etrius' body; when he returned after the Mexico City trip the stake (inscribed with runes, so probably a magical one) was on the ground, and Saulot was gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elder Fortitude could make one immune to staking, or social Disciplines to get someone to pull the stake. Even the old write up of Astral Projection included a sentence about spending a Will (I think?) to become solid for a turn, so that would allow and Astral Projected vampire the ability to pull their own stake out. I\u2019m away from my books, so I don\u2019t know if that wording is still in V20, but Elder levels of Auspex would overcome that anyways.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:05:52-07:00","id":974542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974522#post974522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with this last statement. I think a Nuclear strike will kill any of the Antideluvians that aren't masters of Fotitude or have some other hand wavy power to survive (Vissicitude 10 comes to mind). Even the Fotitude 10 Antes are only surviving because of TT-version Aegis powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the other Antes without Fortitude would not be killable with a nuke.<br /> <br /> Lasombra Obtenebration 10 is an hell of a plot device too, he is bigger than earth and was immune even to the sun, Malkav doesn't simply have a body anymore, Toreador and Brujah could just teleport away with Celerity, Haqim could use that or just be reborn through the blood of his children with quietus, Tremere with Thauma 10 could just summon whatever protection he'd need, Set could use serpentis 10 to become immune to the fire (with Serpentis 9 you can already become immune to the sun).<br /> Only poor Nosfe would have a problem reisting or avoiding the blast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The numbers really don't matter. Like, not even a little bit. And I think it would be 12 levels, not dice. But even then, is it that the damage was multiplied or that there were 4 suns? 4 Suns would be a lot easier to soak, since they would be soaked individually. But again, this stuff happened the way it did because the writers wrote it that way, not because any sort of dice rolling would support it. </div> </div> </div>Yeah maybe they were levels, I should check.<br /> It was the light of the sun amplified 4 times by solar mirrors, so it would be the usual damagex4<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can't actually soak that amount of damage, they just get to magically survive it <i>because plot</i>. </div> </div> </div>It is stated in Gheena that as long as you have blood you can soak anything with Fortitude 10, in fact after being hit by the Nukes Ravnos was hungry for blood.<br /> <br /> Besides when you talk about Ante everything is because plot, Discipline level 10 are just that, Plot, they are like an Archsphere at the maximum level,you can do anything related to that discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Besides there is quite the hint that the Antes are simply immortal and can be killed only by a peer.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius,Lasombra,Tzimisce,Saulot, they all have been physically killed at some point of their unlife.<br /> Not that they cared about it.<br /> <br /> Remember that to make them &quot;killable&quot; Ghenna had to rely on the anti-plot device &quot;the withering&quot;.<br /> Because otherwise is pretty much possible that Antes simply cannot die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:18:37-07:00","id":974550,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974542#post974542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lasombra Obtenebration 10 is an hell of a plot device too, he is bigger than earth and was immune even to the sun, Malkav doesn't simply have a body anymore, Toreador and Brujah could just teleport away with Celerity, Haqim could use that or just be reborn through the blood of his children with quietus, Tremere with Thauma 10 could just summon whatever protection he'd need, Set could use serpentis 10 to become immune to the fire (with Serpentis 9 you can already become immune to the sun).<br /> Only poor Nosfe would have a problem reisting or avoiding the blast.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of those examples are pure speculation. But that's kind of my point. You are deciding they get to survive. It certainly isn't a matter of rolling anything.<br /> <br /> Edit: and as a follow up thought. Half of those examples are avoiding the damage, not surviving it. It\u2019s a different approach. That assumes they are aware of the attack in advance, which with a nuclear assault that very well may not be the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974542#post974542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is stated in Gheena that as long as you have blood you can soak anything with Fortitude 10, in fact after being hit by the Nukes Ravnos was hungry for blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also stated that Ravnos was in frenzy the whole time, which being a master of Animalsim is just kind of pure silliness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974542#post974542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Besides there is quite the hint that the Antes are simply immortal and can be killed only by a peer.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius,Lasombra,Tzimisce,Saulot, they all have been physically killed at some point of their unlife.<br /> Not that they cared about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I tend to find that line of thought to be lazy writing. There is no reason Antes should need a &quot;peer&quot; to destroy them. That's just a way of making sure the players know they can never do anything actionable that will ever make any difference.<br /> <br /> It's funny. I feel like in the Dark Ages, the Antes were presented as much closer &quot;normal&quot; (term used extremely loosely). And then sometime in the last 6-800 years, they all get to transform into nigh unstoppable blood gods. And I accept that that is mostly a matter of writers, but I tend to agree more with the DA portrayal.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:04:44-07:00","id":974755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974390#post974390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, he didn't. He was around four devices that were on par with nukes, but only affected spirits. As vampires are not spirits and have little, if any, connection to them, he wouldn't have been affected as a matter of course, but then again, neither would have a 15th gen neonate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit nukes are full-on nuclear weapons which have been altered via Technocracy magick to affect the Umbra as destructively as they do this side of the Gauntlet. In purely vampire terms it's a pretty meaningless distinction, until you start talking about vampires whose disciplines can and may very well affect the Umbra (and aside from various blood sorceries, Chimerstry -- especially elder-level Chimerstry -- is an A-list candidate).<br /> <br /> Hell, one of the elder-level Chimerstry powers (if I remember right) is basically yanking a Bygone from the Umbra and setting it loose. It's no stretch of the imagination at all to assume the ability to create a Shallowing at will, create a shade realm, or even shift an entire area into the Penumbra (or further beyond) is within the grasp of Chimerstry 10.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, the spirit nukes going off at all was a major concession to the Technocracy, considering one of the Chimerstry 9 powers is the ability to straight-up delete an object from existence, or otherwise render it completely harmless. And that probably didn't happen because Zapathasura had no idea what nuclear weapons were, didn't expect them to be <i>that</i> powerful, or just didn't care.<br /> <br /> <i>[EDIT: Since it came up, both inside and out of the context of the Zapathasura internet slap-fight, one of my default assumptions for Animalism 10 is the Antediluvian is permanently considered a wight for the purposes of resisting mind-affecting powers, soak and wound penalties, and Willpower checks, but retain their morality rating, higher mind function, and personality. In other words, all the strengths and bonuses but none of the weaknesses or drawbacks.]</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-22-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:11:53-07:00","id":975189,"title":"","content":"It might be a little bit less impressive, (within the scope of the discussion at least) if we don't assume that all 4 of the nukes hit at once, (the same &quot;round&quot;), so it's very possible that Ravnos &quot;only&quot; needed to Soak for instance 10 levels of Agg damage, plus 5 levels of Bashing(remember, all vampires half Bashing before soak), and 0-16 lethal damage from radiation (not sure how that would be handled, honestly) at any given time, so anywhere between 15 - 31 levels of damage at once, (which should probably be 3 different rolls as it would involve different Traits to roll to resist), which isn't all that devastating all in all, (again considering it's an Antediluvian).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the &quot;so it does 10 levels of aggravated damages in a radius of 140 meters&quot; and the &quot;plus 10 dice of aggravated damages in the range of 350 meters&quot; are meant to stack, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 09-23-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:51:03-07:00","id":975257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=975189#post975189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be a little bit less impressive, (within the scope of the discussion at least) if we don't assume that all 4 of the nukes hit at once, (the same &quot;round&quot;), so it's very possible that Ravnos &quot;only&quot; needed to Soak for instance 10 levels of Agg damage, plus 5 levels of Bashing(remember, all vampires half Bashing before soak), and 0-16 lethal damage from radiation (not sure how that would be handled, honestly) at any given time, so anywhere between 15 - 31 levels of damage at once, (which should probably be 3 different rolls as it would involve different Traits to roll to resist), which isn't all that devastating all in all, (again considering it's an Antediluvian).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the &quot;so it does 10 levels of aggravated damages in a radius of 140 meters&quot; and the &quot;plus 10 dice of aggravated damages in the range of 350 meters&quot; are meant to stack, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never made vampires suffer damage from radiation, personally. Acute or chronic radiation sickness is based upon one thing: the target having a metabolism in the first place. If it's a massive enough dose to start damaging (non-living) matter, honestly, the <i>source</i> of that dosage is going to be the problem, not the dosage itself. In other words, dump a vampire into the core of a purely hypothetical, active, nuclear reactor, and they'll die to &quot;fire/heat&quot; damage long before the radiation has its chance.<br /> <br /> <i>That said</i>, I've always played Fortitude 10 to be &quot;The vampire adds their Stamina + Fortitude as additional health levels, and all health levels except for Incapacitated convert to &quot;bruised&quot; (i.e. they never suffer wound penalties). The vampire's soak pool against any form of damage is Stamina + Fortitude, including fire or sunlight, and the vampire soaks at maximum difficulty 6. Spend a Willpower point to ignore any single source of damage which would incapacitate or kill the vampire, after soak. Spend a blood point to ignore any other attack which deals damage after soak.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:59:18-07:00","id":975282,"title":"","content":"Antediluvians are quasi-mythical plot devices/bogeymen that players in my game will never meet and may or may not ever rise (unless I ever run the TC or GS again). Their disciplines are subtle plot devices. Why bother to give them stats? That just reduces the game to 1st ed D&amp;D where Deities and Demigods had stats for the Gods, and players could &quot;combat&quot; them. It's just dumb, because at any point a player could actually challenge a &quot;God&quot; stat-wise in Vampire, D&amp;D, etc., the game has devolved into a parody of itself.<br /> <br /> From the Giovanni Chronicles:<br /> Cappadocius<br /> To provide Traits for Cappadocius would be ridiculous. No one in this story could affect him without his permission.<br /> <br /> That includes Japheth and Augustus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5853-krb","name":"KRB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T18:36:19-07:00","id":975323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KRB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=975282#post975282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antediluvians are quasi-mythical plot devices/bogeymen...the game has devolved into a parody of itself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for anyone else, but I do it for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> One, Antediluvians <i>can</i> and <i>have</i> shown up in my games. Hell, I ran an MtA story <i>about</i> the rise (and defeat) of [Tzimisce]. That story also included Arikel, and for like a half-second, Tremere. It does, in fact, help to be able to provide some quantifiable limit and expectation of level 10 disciplines, both to plan the story and shape it as it develops (how Character A, that being an Antediluvian in this context, would cause or react to Scenario B within the confines of their power and character). Because players -- or at least, <i>my</i> players -- have a strong tendency to call bullshit on anything which strains suspension of disbelief on grounds of depth, scale, or character-breaking.<br /> <br /> Two and Three, but placed together because they're very similar in intent, it makes an excellent thought experiment. I find it helps to learn game mechanics better, and what <i>can</i> and <i>cannot</i> be done under normal circumstances within the confines of the game's rules. Believe it or not, I've actually worked out pretty good Master- and Archmaster-level magickal Effects based upon ideas I've had for level 8, 9, and even 10 discipline use, and vice versa. But, that's my perspective as an almost exclusively Mage and Vampire player; I'm sure Werewolf players might find fertile imaginative ground for Incarna and Celestines, as well as more flamboyant Legend-level Gifts, as an example.<br /> <br /> Plus, for those of us who like playing with Elder-level powers (either on a purely creative level, or in the course of actual gameplay) and creating their own, imagining how a level 10 power might look thematically and mechanically provides an upper boundary by comparison for level 9 powers, and so on down the line. That sense of perspective is important when planning, testing, and balancing homebrew Elder-level powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:27:12-07:00","id":975529,"title":"","content":"Closest thing I've seen to a statted Antediluvian is a horribly powerful Earthbound from Demon: The Fallen. Except minus the limits on its power regarding other Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T00:03:43-07:00","id":975862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=974292#post974292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes no sense, both rules-wise and plot-wise.<br /> Baba Yaga is nowhere near an Antediluvian,to fight Nosferatu she had to summon six amazingly powerful Dragons, plus one of the Wyrm's Talons,Koshchey the deathless.<br /> Antediluvian are on Incarna or Oracles level of power, no methuselah can beat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are making my point for me. <br /> <br /> She summoned six of the most powerful Wyrm creatures ever to walk the earth. She did this during her first hour as a vampire. Then she summoned a TALON OF THE WYRM straight out of his prison. Something no one... not pentex, not an antediluvian, hell, not even the Wyrm itself has been able to do. She smashed through the prison that the legendary garou had bound Koshchei into, and called it to her on the spot. Successfully resisting Absimiliard as a day old fledgling. <br /> <br /> And I agree with you that Incarna are on par with the Antediluvians. Don't forget that one of them works for Baba Yaga (Typhon)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lol, Ravnos withstood four nuclear strikes, a tank shell would bother and Antediluvian just like a fly could bother an elephant. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and many consider that battle the most poorly written event in the history of the World of Darkness (it's up there with Baba Yaga's death). Most gamers I know stopped playing World of Darkness games at around that time, because the writing and supplements were just getting too stupid.<br /> <br /> The death of Ravnos marks the transition of the World of Darkness going from a setting of Gothic Punk Horror, to one of a Big Eyes, Small Mouth, anime style Cartoon setting... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12215-godslayer","name":"Godslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:13:05-07:00","id":976115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=975862#post975862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The death of Ravnos marks the transition of the World of Darkness going from a setting of Gothic Punk Horror, to one of a Big Eyes, Small Mouth, anime style Cartoon setting...</div> </div> </div> </div>That same &quot;Gothic Punk Horror&quot; setting had shit like the old Tal'mahe'Ra and Soul-Eaters, fae-blooded Malkavians, and Sam Haight. Yet somehow the Week of Nightmares was the problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T21:28:05-07:00","id":976343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=938939#post938939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, they are powerful enough that it takes 13 4th generation vampires to bind them, and they have to be supported by 169 ghouls that they have specially trained. The Antediluvians have perfect immortality. If killed, they will reform within a thousand years. If diabolorized, they will take control of their attacker within a century (Cappadocious is an exception because he wanted to become God and found, too late, that God does not exist, at least not on any level that an Antediluvian can access). The only way to stop them is to ritually imprison them with the previously mentioned ritual, body and soul, after draining them completely of Vitae and staking them. Even then, they will eventually escape after ten thousand years (or sooner, if anyone bothers the iron wrapped tungsten coffins that my NPCs used to prevent the Week of Nightmares).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that's the case, then how did they destroy the second generation?<br /> <br /> And what happens if the second generation suddenly comes back to life?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:02:40-07:00","id":976397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976343#post976343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If that's the case, then how did they destroy the second generation?<br /> <br /> And what happens if the second generation suddenly comes back to life?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They where diablerized and have long ago taken control of their new body but kept quiet about it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:55:30-07:00","id":976415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976343#post976343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If that's the case, then how did they destroy the second generation?<br /> <br /> And what happens if the second generation suddenly comes back to life?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The curse of Weakening down the Generations was imposed by Caine after the Second Generation were destroyed, no? The Third Generation were of equal power to the Second Generation, as far as I can recall.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, our current Third Generation Vampires have existed for thousands of years. On a relative scale compared to that, the Second Generation and the Third Generation were basically the same age. Then factor in that the Third Generation outnumber them, and it seems reasonable that they would be beaten. The Eldest had run off before that point, and Ventru refused to take part, and Saulot was also gone by that point, but that still leaves ten against three (unless any other clan has a &quot;oh no Our Progenitor was super duper honorable and had no part in the betrayal&quot; myth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T03:30:02-07:00","id":976444,"title":"","content":"Well they have origin myths placing them in other parts of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:11:55-07:00","id":976459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976444#post976444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they have origin myths placing them in other parts of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>However those are Myths. The Setites think Set is a Gen 2. They think that Ra created the other 12 Antedeluvians to give Set Rivals. They sometimes think Set was the first Vampire, or that he's something beyond a Vampire.<br /> <br /> Some Ravnos think that their Antedeluvian is a Gen 2. They also have origin myths which deny all of the others.<br /> <br /> As far as I am aware, the &quot;truth&quot; is that all 13 of the Gen 3s (the 13 who survived the Flood and created Clans at least) were known to Caine and were all known to eachother. The Eldest is an odd point, as it is possible that he abandoned the City before even being introduced to the other Gen 3s, I can't really recall the exact details on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T05:06:46-07:00","id":976473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976459#post976459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However those are Myths. The Setites think Set is a Gen 2. They think that Ra created the other 12 Antedeluvians to give Set Rivals. They sometimes think Set was the first Vampire, or that he's something beyond a Vampire.<br /> <br /> Some Ravnos think that their Antedeluvian is a Gen 2. They also have origin myths which deny all of the others.<br /> <br /> As far as I am aware, the &quot;truth&quot; is that all 13 of the Gen 3s (the 13 who survived the Flood and created Clans at least) were known to Caine and were all known to eachother. The Eldest is an odd point, as it is possible that he abandoned the City before even being introduced to the other Gen 3s, I can't really recall the exact details on that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Setites believe Set is a Gen 1. They are not descendants of Cain the Vampire, they're descendants of Set, the God. Setites count themselves as being 2 generations lower than normal, because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:10:00-07:00","id":976487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976473#post976473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Setites believe Set is a Gen 1. They are not descendants of Cain the Vampire, they're descendants of Set, the God. Setites count themselves as being 2 generations lower than normal, because of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well different Setites believe different things. They have multiple origin myths in circulation (even Lore of the Clans has three) and they aren't all meant to be interpreted literally. I doubt any sensible Setite genuinely believes that they aren't Cainites. If they weren't they wouldn't be subject to exactly the same Curses as the other Clans, nor would they have compatible powers and the ability to Diablerise them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:17:04-07:00","id":976491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976487#post976487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt any sensible Setite genuinely believes that they aren't Cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think you understand how <i>cults</i> work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:24:36-07:00","id":976493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976491#post976491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you understand how <i>cults</i> work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming that Setites are all fundamentalists. The recurring theme in the Cult of Sutekh is it's philosophy and Modus Operandi. It isn't a group which screams &quot;this factual information is definitely true, this is the only truth&quot;. Again, read Lore of the Clans. The chapter on Setites has a stereotypical Setite Narrator offer up three possible origins and not present any of them as fact, outright calling them Stories. You know, the way many cults and religious denominations actually work. Fundamentalism is assumed to be old-fashioned and near-universal, but IIRC Setites have never been presented as Fundamentalists. If you want Fundamentalism, look to the Ba'hari and the Followers of Caine. For them it's their way or the highway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:47:22-07:00","id":976515,"title":"","content":"Of course, a lot of Setites do believe that they are descendants of a god of darkness, rather than the third mortal, because it makes a better story. They see no particular reason to believe in Caine (or the Abrahamic religious point-of-view) because they do not get anything from it. In fact, I imagine that Setites just love to use logical and scientific arguments to disprove the Abrahamic beliefs of their neonates, all the while presenting the Setite beliefs as highly symbolic versions of the truth (which are probably subtlety edited to reflect new scientific discoveries when there is a direct conflict).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:19:18-07:00","id":976623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KRB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=975282#post975282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antediluvians are quasi-mythical plot devices/bogeymen that players in my game will never meet and may or may not ever rise (unless I ever run the TC or GS again). Their disciplines are subtle plot devices. Why bother to give them stats? That just reduces the game to 1st ed D&amp;D where Deities and Demigods had stats for the Gods, and players could &quot;combat&quot; them. It's just dumb, because at any point a player could actually challenge a &quot;God&quot; stat-wise in Vampire, D&amp;D, etc., the game has devolved into a parody of itself.<br /> <br /> From the Giovanni Chronicles:<br /> Cappadocius<br /> To provide Traits for Cappadocius would be ridiculous. No one in this story could affect him without his permission.<br /> <br /> That includes Japheth and Augustus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm, we could disagree on that. I don't feel the urge to statting out antes, because 9 times out of 10 they won't came up in a chronicle, just as most D&amp;D campaigns don't go into plane-spanning, gods-toppling territory. But on the one time it does...<br /> <br /> Let's say, I just like more the notion of ridiculously powerful, but still beatable adversaries, than unbeatable blood-gods (or gods in D&amp;D for that matter, If in the setting's backstory gods are died and mortals make it to godhood, then why on Earth the characters shouldn't be able to???).<br /> <br /> It just breaks my verisimilitude, when the characters can't stand a chance, not because the powergap for duking out face-to-face (and which is therefore could be cheated in a lot of ways), but because they are gods and therefore no one could fight them, not even their progeny and not even in superior numbers, or the mightiest garou, or archmasters, because they are antes, and our dick is the biggest, period. My personal taste in the case of most rpgs is &quot;everyone could die&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unless we speak about Lovecraftian cosmic horror, which I also like, but then it is the whole point and style of that and i just don't feel it necessary for the aspect of horror WoD caters to in my mind. The feeling of powerlessness is important to horror, but it could be created in a lot of ways and saying &quot;you just can't fight these guys&quot; is honestly, one of the cheapest methods and even contradicts with the setting's backstory IMO.<br /> <br /> But then again, I never liked the idea of Gehenna as the honest to goodness End of the World.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-26-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:28:16-07:00","id":976629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976459#post976459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I am aware, the &quot;truth&quot; is that all 13 of the Gen 3s (the 13 who survived the Flood and created Clans at least) were known to Caine and were all known to eachother. The Eldest is an odd point, as it is possible that he abandoned the City before even being introduced to the other Gen 3s, I can't really recall the exact details on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware there is no &quot;truth.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:31:25-07:00","id":976660,"title":"","content":"The Antes, having once been human and still having humanoid features, also don't work very well as lovecraftian adversaries. Incomprehensibility and obfuscation of nature/purpose/origin are pretty key to that aesthetic- it doesn't work once you've explained things or made them relatable. Earthbound *barely* work in a lovecraftian sense (they're honestly more just a whimsical reference in that component of their fluff)- the Neverborn are pretty solid for it I suppose (.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:35:50-07:00","id":976663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976623#post976623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhm, we could disagree on that. I don't feel the urge to statting out antes, because 9 times out of 10 they won't came up in a chronicle, just as most D&amp;D campaigns don't go into plane-spanning, gods-toppling territory. But on the one time it does...<br /> <br /> Let's say, I just like more the notion of ridiculously powerful, but still beatable adversaries, than unbeatable blood-gods (or gods in D&amp;D for that matter, If in the setting's backstory gods are died and mortals make it to godhood, then why on Earth the characters shouldn't be able to???).<br /> <br /> It just breaks my verisimilitude, when the characters can't stand a chance, not because the powergap for duking out face-to-face (and which is therefore could be cheated in a lot of ways), but because they are gods and therefore no one could fight them, not even their progeny and not even in superior numbers, or the mightiest garou, or archmasters, because they are antes, and our dick is the biggest, period. My personal taste in the case of most rpgs is &quot;everyone could die&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unless we speak about Lovecraftian cosmic horror, which I also like, but then it is the whole point and style of that and i just don't feel it necessary for the aspect of horror WoD caters to in my mind. The feeling of powerlessness is important to horror, but it could be created in a lot of ways and saying &quot;you just can't fight these guys&quot; is honestly, one of the cheapest methods and even contradicts with the setting's backstory IMO.<br /> <br /> But then again, I never liked the idea of Gehenna as the honest to goodness End of the World.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In D&amp;D, a god can only be permanently slain inside its own plane of power, which is where it is most powerful. And mortals can't become gods without the approval of Ao, who is an allegory for the Dungeon Master. So while it is technically possible to accomplish both feats, it is really, really hard to do so!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:43:38-07:00","id":976667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976660#post976660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Antes, having once been human and still having humanoid features, also don't work very well as lovecraftian adversaries. Incomprehensibility and obfuscation of nature/purpose/origin are pretty key to that aesthetic- it doesn't work once you've explained things or made them relatable. Earthbound *barely* work in a lovecraftian sense (they're honestly more just a whimsical reference in that component of their fluff)- the Neverborn are pretty solid for it I suppose (.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well actually, the Antes may have been human, but thousands of years of vampirism has turned them into something completely different. The Tzimisce, for example, discovered a way to hyper accelerate evolution, and is now a giant, chimerical biomass living underneath New York.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Ante is in a similar boat, as Cain warped him to a point he's not even recognizable as human anymore, and he went onto create a horde of similarly twisted monsters to carry out his will.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lasombra ante became a creature of living darkness after repeated explorations at the bottom of the sea.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the Ravnos ante literally drove everybody insane for a week.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any of these sound pretty in theme with Lovecraft Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:56:45-07:00","id":976675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976663#post976663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In D&amp;D, a god can only be permanently slain inside its own plane of power, which is where it is most powerful. And mortals can't become gods without the approval of Ao, who is an allegory for the Dungeon Master. So while it is technically possible to accomplish both feats, it is really, really hard to do so!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quite right in the case of FR. Other worlds and games have different ways, like the Starstone in Golarion.<br /> <br /> And as one of the characters in the latest Brimstone Angels book said &quot;Gods die all the time.&quot; Netheril, Time of Troubles, Spellplague, Sundering. D&amp;D and most of it's worlds are just not really places when gods are ultimate permanents of the universe. They really are just very-very-very strong entities. I do agree however that the whole god-slaying and becoming one is pretty much DM caveat, but i still think it is the part of the game and its settings as written.<br /> <br /> I think along the same lines about antes. Are they ridiculously powerful? Yes. Should the simultaneous waking of a bunch of them (since some of them were active all the time or with intermissions) shake the kindred society? Yes, absolutely. Are they killable? Oh, yes, it's just hard as hell, but it happened before. They are among the strongest entities of the WoD, but even they could fall, given the right circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:00:44-07:00","id":976678,"title":"","content":"Well, strictly speaking the Gods weren't actually &quot;Gods&quot; during the Time of Troubles. Ao kicked them out and made them all mortal. Hence why they were able to die. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:12:51-07:00","id":976689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976678#post976678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, strictly speaking the Gods weren't actually &quot;Gods&quot; during the Time of Troubles. Ao kicked them out and made them all mortal. Hence why they were able to die. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And if I recall correctly, Mysrtill (or what was her name at that time) was dead for a short period when Karsus ascended. Later, during the spellplague, a lot of gods get killed. You might dislike it, or exclude it from your Realms, but it is a part of the canonical setting, gods could die and could be killed.<br /> <br /> As for the antes whom transcended the vampiric state to some extent: in those case my standpoint is still more like &quot;how could we kill THAT?&quot; than &quot;nope, you couldn't, that's it.&quot; Honestly, my opinion is that those ones are more akin to spirits at this point. Find the weakness and they'll fall.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:14:36-07:00","id":976691,"title":"","content":"Well, no, because we know the backstories of the Antes and can conceptualize their former human personalities- moreover a number of them like Arikel, Troile, etc. never became truly alien. It just doesn't really work- we know of the men they once were, often have a notion of their trajectory and of the personalities of the things that created them, etc. There's no real element of truly unknowable, alien horror here- Lasombra and Tzimisce are just extremes of mindsets that exist even among modern vampires that PCs can even personally choose to adopt i.e. Road of the Abyss, Path of Metamorphosis, etc. (and Lasombra is depicted as a pathetic creature whom the real horrors of the Abyss look upon with in contempt, so that's not really very impressive in that sense either). They're just extremes of a common playing field rather than anything fundamentally outside any PC level entity's ability to conceptualize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:25:05-07:00","id":976757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976691#post976691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, because we know the backstories of the Antes and can conceptualize their former human personalities- moreover a number of them like Arikel, Troile, etc. never became truly alien. It just doesn't really work- we know of the men they once were, often have a notion of their trajectory and of the personalities of the things that created them, etc. There's no real element of truly unknowable, alien horror here- Lasombra and Tzimisce are just extremes of mindsets that exist even among modern vampires that PCs can even personally choose to adopt i.e. Road of the Abyss, Path of Metamorphosis, etc. (and Lasombra is depicted as a pathetic creature whom the real horrors of the Abyss look upon with in contempt, so that's not really very impressive in that sense either). They're just extremes of a common playing field rather than anything fundamentally outside any PC level entity's ability to conceptualize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, we only have the claims of their childer that they were born human. For all we known, they are Lovecraftian monstrosities who were punished by their peers by trapping them in human bodies for eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:18:38-07:00","id":976816,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and maybe they're also extremely empathetic fluffy pink unicorns from space who have been slandered by their insolent progeny, given that there are no external precedents for earthshaking cosmic horrors possessing clad in human flesh being embraceable in-setting. You either go with the moderately consistent legends or in the Gehenna supplement objective-ish stuff or you go with nothing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 09-26-2016, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:53:06-07:00","id":976841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976757#post976757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, we only have the claims of their childer that they were born human. For all we known, they are Lovecraftian monstrosities who were punished by their peers by trapping them in human bodies for eternity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Plus, the Setites believe their Antedeluvian was a literal god.<br /> <br /> And the Baali progenitors were demon worshipers long before they became vampires.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:56:26-07:00","id":977370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=976691#post976691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lasombra is depicted as a pathetic creature whom the real horrors of the Abyss look upon with in contempt</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, Lovecraft's mythology refers to Azathoth as the <b>Idiot God.</b> When you openly call one of the most powerful beings in your pantheon an idiot, I don't think Lasombra being looked upon as pathetic is much of a disparagement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:16:23-07:00","id":977388,"title":"","content":"I suspect, from the viewpoint of the creatures of the Abyss, Lasombra is an upstart wannabe. He is just a vampire after all.<br /> <br /> Just as, from the viewpoint of real mages, especially archmasters, the Tremere and their thaumaturgy is a joke, a pale shadow and mockery of awakened magick.<br /> <br /> I also suspect all of them are committing the biggest mistake you could about vampires: underestimating them. Lasombra might not be a &quot;real&quot; creature of the Abyss, but he is something more as much as something less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-27-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:55:22-07:00","id":977416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=977388#post977388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect, from the viewpoint of the creatures of the Abyss, Lasombra is an upstart wannabe. He is just a vampire after all.<br /> <br /> Just as, from the viewpoint of real mages, especially archmasters, the Tremere and their thaumaturgy is a joke, a pale shadow and mockery of awakened magick.<br /> <br /> I also suspect all of them are committing the biggest mistake you could about vampires: underestimating them. Lasombra might not be a &quot;real&quot; creature of the Abyss, but he is something more as much as something less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Lasombra a special case? He's only powerful insofar as he has become a literal tool of the force of the Abyss. He &quot;wants&quot; to end existence, being a mere puppet of the force which stands against light and order, however his power is only something he is a relay for. He's about as powerful as someone using Daimoinon 8 to call forth a Hellbound. That's little comfort to those who stand against him, however it's worth noting. It isn't really his power. There are other cases of this; certain Elder Baali and Dark Thaumaturges who are just conduits for Demons, certain Necromancers who want to tear down the veil but are unknowingly puppets of that one Archmage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:05:13-07:00","id":977422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=977388#post977388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect, from the viewpoint of the creatures of the Abyss, Lasombra is an upstart wannabe. He is just a vampire after all.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And Cthulhu is just a priest, not even an actual God! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-27-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T21:54:16-07:00","id":993884,"title":"","content":"The gap between the 4th and the 3rd generation is supposed to be big. The biggest gap we know about is between the 7th and the 6th generation. Blood pool increases by 50% from 20 to 30, and 4 BP per round to 6.<br /> <br /> So, the gap between the 4th and the 3rd should be the same, as should the gap between the 2nd and the 1st. The gap between 3rd and 2nd would be more akin to that between the 5th and the 4th.<br /> <br /> So, since 4th Gens have 50 blood points and can spend 10 per round<br /> <br /> 3rd Gens - 75 BP, 15 BP per round<br /> 2nd Gens - 100 BP, 20 BP per round<br /> Caine - 150 BP, 30 BP per round<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:02:58-07:00","id":994206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=993884#post993884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since 4th Gens have 50 blood points and can spend 10 per round<br /> <br /> 3rd Gens - 75 BP, 15 BP per round<br /> 2nd Gens - 100 BP, 20 BP per round<br /> Caine - 150 BP, 30 BP per round</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I've been saying that since literally 1991, when the game came out. (Of course, there are other power-facets attributable to the Caine-thru-3rd generations that transcend numerics, but the vitae/BP ratios pretty much hold out in most metaphysical contexts...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:17:10-07:00","id":994212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=993884#post993884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gap between the 4th and the 3rd generation is supposed to be big. The biggest gap we know about is between the 7th and the 6th generation. Blood pool increases by 50% from 20 to 30, and 4 BP per round to 6.<br /> <br /> So, the gap between the 4th and the 3rd should be the same, as should the gap between the 2nd and the 1st. The gap between 3rd and 2nd would be more akin to that between the 5th and the 4th.<br /> <br /> So, since 4th Gens have 50 blood points and can spend 10 per round<br /> <br /> 3rd Gens - 75 BP, 15 BP per round<br /> 2nd Gens - 100 BP, 20 BP per round<br /> Caine - 150 BP, 30 BP per round</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the 3rd Gens should be more like 100BP and 20 per round, a more exponential sorta jump rather than par for the course. Caine should simply be whatever he wants, and it will use blood against his will to keep him alive while mystically stealing blood from whatever is around him to fuel the curse (like Alucard perhaps) since he's the ultimate cursed and he isn't supposed to be able to reach final death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:32:59-07:00","id":994273,"title":"","content":"Mmmh...can Antedeluvians pump their stats via blood over 10 dots?<br /> Lets just assume they can use 20 bp per turn, can they pump their strenght to 30?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T20:22:29-07:00","id":994366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=994273#post994273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmh...can Antedeluvians pump their stats via blood over 10 dots?<br /> Lets just assume they can use 20 bp per turn, can they pump their strenght to 30?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would doubt it...but if they had Strength 10 and Potence 10 they could be rolling 10 dice of strength with 10 automatic successes on top of that. But I look at 10 as the hard limit on everything. Only Caine could feasibly act beyond it in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:27:02-07:00","id":994430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=994206#post994206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconded. I've been saying that since literally 1991, when the game came out. (Of course, there are other power-facets attributable to the Caine-thru-3rd generations that transcend numerics, but the vitae/BP ratios pretty much hold out in most metaphysical contexts...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, I've been using that formula since 1999 when the blood pool of an Antediluvian actually become relevant for a game.<br /> <br /> Granted, my Antediluvians are more like Third Circle Demons from Exalted in their power level than any vampires, making them able to use this blood pool to lay down the smack on basically anything that isn't a huge Technocratic elite strike force with only the best gear like the one used during the Week of Nightmares, or an actual, literal army of werewolves willing to die to take the damn Wyrm-creature down.<br /> <br /> Like, Arikel introduced itself by going &quot;lol fuck you, any remote-guided weapons can't get a lock on me, get fucked Union&quot;, and Ravana basically spent the entire battle going &quot;lol I wasn't there anyways, you hit your own targets, quit shooting yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Likewise, if I ever introduce Tremere (which may be a possibility soon), he'll start out by burning a city block to ashes in a few seconds, and he wont <i>need</i> to be statless in order to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T10:22:20-08:00","id":1473758,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest power in the Antes is to control their children. For me, no Blood Bond is the same as the one with your forefather/mothers, and they can simply can command or subtly affect their descendants. So if you really want to destroy an Antediluvian level Cainite, it either must permit you, or you will need the help of other lineages. Divide and Conquer is really the biggest advantage and chance of success to challenge the 3rd gen. But hell, Antes are so alien and lost in their own millenniums-long ambitions and plans that they probably out of themselves and not really lucid. <br /> <br /> Yes they can and have been killed. Thirteen have just been the most prolific, and some of them were cannibalized, while other 'clans' of ancient times were eradicated or made so small nobody knows or cares; hell, there might be some on a Masquerade against other vampires just to survive them (like Inconnu or that group of weirdos in BJD). But they have been dead, and from some only echoes remains, cuz the power of the Blood and their Curse don't just disappear, they spread, and so might their mandates.<br /> <br /> We don't talk about the Beasts of the Antediluvians, but I also don't see them following Paths, but their Banes and Beasts would be insurmountable. So something happened... Who knows, maybe their banes were simply ways to let their Beasts empty their strength, or to really bind them. Or maybe Caine (or whoever) did it, but for similar reasons. Either way, I also think something happened, like, I believe there is a pact of some sorts between the Antediluvians. Like of mutual non-aggressions, even if just after the 2nd City. So they can't really fight each other, just scheme with their childer. And hell, maybe it goes further, maybe Nod and Caine is all a big freaking sham.<br /> <br /> Maybe the known Antes are really just old Methuselahs who nobody can prove are not the founders. Cuz yeah, for me the power between Methus and Antes is really close. And both are alienated and incomprehensible, and don't care anymore to be so; Japphet and Cappadocius tried to be understood , but the Children of Isaac and Camarilla and everyone else just thought &quot;I don't get it, it seems really big and bad, just better be safe and fuck it, get this old man out of here&quot;. And so they let thigs play out and maybe it worked and we are just to ignorant, or maybe we screwed up their plans, and will never know if it would indeed be better. <br /> <br /> In the end, they are like trying to understand the origin of life on Earth, you may get some really good theories and ideas and proofs, but hell, it is so hard to interpret. And worst, you can't even investigate very well, cuz much of this was manufactured and/or falsely stated, and for a society that lives in the shadows of humanity you can't expect clarity and true-to-facts history (cuz that doesn't really exist).<br /> But they are a fun concept and theme to explore. Especially because everyone has a different idea, and my PCs can see clearly that someone of thousands of years has a lot of different lives, characters and faces. And some of the strongest themes for ancient vampires and the young ones is that of history repeating, the curse of patricide and fratricide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T13:35:51-08:00","id":1473770,"title":"","content":"Their stat block is 'you lose'. Mind you most Methuselah share that stat block, the power level comparison:. Caine is a Tsar Bomb The Antes are Castle Bravo, and the Meths top out at B53 gravity bomb level devastation, if you are the focus of any of these options you won't even be a shadow on the wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T14:09:19-08:00","id":1473774,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;How powerful are yours?&quot;</i><br /> As powerful as the pcs believe them to be<br /> <i>&quot;What can they do?&quot;</i><br /> Whatever the characters imagine they can and credit them with.<br /> <i>&quot;What CAN'T they do?&quot;</i><br /> Actually turn up in a story except in rumours of their involvement.<br /> <i>&quot;And what does it take to kill one?&quot;</i><br /> The end of existence, as they're either intrinsically bound to some facet of existence itself and beyond mortal reach and comprehension (such as the Abyss, or the Earth itself, or whatever), or they're an idea that never actually existed in the first place and vampiric society is just a big paranoid superstitious mess so they'll stop existing when you stop thinking they do.<br /> -<br /> The Antedeluvians - and their power levels - should forever stay a mystery, as far as I'm concerned. They're more effective that way.<br /> Maybe they're pulling the strings behind politics. Maybe it's a garden variety methuselah or elder. Maybe you're just paraoid.<br /> The horrific and confusing events that sometimes take place, leaving death and destruction in their wake, might be the end times and maybe it's just a bad Tuesday. I will never explain anything, just leave little hints that might just be lies.<br /> <br /> If I decided to confirm their existence with their turning up, there would be no fighting them.<br /> A) they aren't going to fight you because they don't actually realise you exist in anything more than an abstract way. Like you know air particles are a thing, and you might send them flying when you exhaule, but you don't really perceive them on your level of existence.<br /> B) As said; merged with cosmic forces. Pick a fist fight with the sun for all the effect you'd have.<br /> <br /> (We do not acknowledge the Week of Nightmares under my roof. That was all one giant reality-exploding fever dream due to unknown mystical forces. The Ravnos are fine. And Cappadocius was actually never the real ante for the Clan of Death. &quot;Who was then?&quot; &quot;How was Cappadocius 3rd generation?&quot; We just don't know. It's one of nature's mysteries. The deity Hekate. It's the founder Clan of <i>Death</i>, man, dying and growing a new one is totally in theme for them. etc, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 02-01-2022, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T07:58:41-08:00","id":1473827,"title":"","content":"Antediluvians are strong enough to get effortlessly curbstomped by Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T15:21:54-08:00","id":1473870,"title":"","content":"Bringing an Ante in is essentially bringing in a god-tier character. I can't imagine any PCs ever fighting them, but they might have to deal with the chaos one or more of them create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T05:20:31-08:00","id":1474189,"title":"","content":"If as some books say, generation gap appeared after 3rd gens\u2019 curse, then Caine, 2nd and 3rd may have same maximum and the only difference is age \u2014 maybe Caine himself isn\u2019t more powerful than his children and grandchildren","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T19:24:00-08:00","id":1474245,"title":"","content":"The Antes were originally fairly blatant expies of The Great Old Ones. They were cosmically invincible beings who would bring madness and death to the world at some ambiguous point in the future. Since they've retconned Gehenna into some cyclical thing that barely attracts human notice I'm not sure what purpose they serve anymore. If the WOD is no longer even partly &quot;Call of Chthulu, but with vampires&quot;, then you might just as well kill the Antes off. Would it even effect anything anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:05:24-08:00","id":1474247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474245#post1474245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Antes were originally fairly blatant expies of The Great Old Ones. They were cosmically invincible beings who would bring madness and death to the world at some ambiguous point in the future. Since they've retconned Gehenna into some cyclical thing that barely attracts human notice I'm not sure what purpose they serve anymore. If the WOD is no longer even partly &quot;Call of Chthulu, but with vampires&quot;, then you might just as well kill the Antes off. Would it even effect anything anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're far more like Akasha from Queen of the Damned.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I think the Antediluvians underscore something that sometimes go over the fandom of some more secular raised individuals. They provide a <i>religious</i> element to vampire that's actually independent of God or the Bible despite Caine. The vampires are all linked by heritage and these mythical monsters of their past that might someday come to kill them. I don't think that you actually ever have to FIRE the Checov's gun of Gehenna, though, and it was probably a mistake to do so. It's more valuable just being there as a constant worry in the back of your mind.<br /> <br /> You can't ever escape Gehenna or the Antediluvians and they're always going to be more powerful than you so a vampire, no matter how evil or selfish or powerful, can never be 100% safe.<br /> <br /> If you're into roleplaying vampirism as awesome, you have that sobering factoid: &quot;I am never going to be the Big Dog in this prison. I'm just a mid-level convict. Can I even trust my own thoughts?&quot;<br /> <br /> And sleeping monsters or not, they've never been too much like the Old Ones because (unless you're like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> who is great), they're not ALIEN per se. They're just the worst of humanity and older than dirt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-09-2022, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T07:40:06-08:00","id":1474373,"title":"","content":"My Antediluvians all have Necromancy 7: the power to resurrect threads long past. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I don't have antediluvians. The oldest existing vampire -- and probably the closest thing to an antediluvian -- in my game is a Gangrel named Dilgan. He's an inner circle member of the Camarilla, and he has 52 dots in disciplines.<br /> <br /> Animalism 7<br /> Fortitude 8<br /> Protean 8<br /> Sharusin 6 (homebrew Gangrel in-clan discipline)<br /> Potence 5<br /> Auspex 5<br /> Obfuscate 5<br /> Thamaturgy Paths:<br /> Blood 4<br /> Vitae's Calling 4 (homebrew path)<br /> <br /> But he has a number of &quot;alternative&quot; disciplines as well, so this doesn't quite tell the whole story. (Example: my game has multiple Auspex 3 options, Auspex 3A, 3B, and 3C. Dilgan has two of those.)<br /> <br /> If the PCs were really smart, they could probably take him. Not in a fair fight, certainly... but even with Fortitude bumped up in power the way it is in my games, it's <i><b>probably </b></i>not going to save you from getting slammed with a volley of BLU-188/Bs in the middle of the day then mobbed by ghouls armed with anti-tank weapons and napalm.<br /> <br /> But it <i><b>might</b></i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T15:01:04-08:00","id":1474443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474245#post1474245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Antes were originally fairly blatant expies of The Great Old Ones. They were cosmically invincible beings who would bring madness and death to the world at some ambiguous point in the future. Since they've retconned Gehenna into some cyclical thing that barely attracts human notice I'm not sure what purpose they serve anymore. If the WOD is no longer even partly &quot;Call of Chthulu, but with vampires&quot;, then you might just as well kill the Antes off. Would it even effect anything anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Bronze_Age_collapse\" target=\"_blank\">Barely</a> attracts human notice? i <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Death\" target=\"_blank\">beg to differ</a>, at least a little.<br /> <br /> And speaking of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Call_of_Cthulhu#Plot_summary\" target=\"_blank\"><i>cosmically invincible</i> </a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schooner\" target=\"_blank\">Great Old Ones</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> meh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-11-2022, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T20:28:49-08:00","id":1474886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474443#post1474443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And speaking of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Call_of_Cthulhu#Plot_summary\" target=\"_blank\"><i>cosmically invincible</i> </a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schooner\" target=\"_blank\">Great Old Ones</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> meh</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the idea that cosmic horror monsters are suppose to be invincible is a pretty modern one.<br /> <br /> Hell, The 10 dot abilities of the ante's used to be described as late as 2nd edition, and they weren't even the out there. Powerful yeah, but powerful in the &quot;I can use a undead army to conquer New York&quot; or &quot;I can send vague dreams to the masses of sleeping people on the other side of the world&quot;, kind of powerful. They were not &quot;I can take on the combined might of humankind(or even just vampire-kind)&quot; level of powerful, which lined up neatly with the need for having a Masquerade in the first place. Making them into unknowable I-Win buttons for the ST, kind of forgets that little tidbit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T04:19:50-08:00","id":1474893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474886#post1474886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the idea that cosmic horror monsters are suppose to be invincible is a pretty modern one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too true and felt the urge to lampshade it a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474886#post1474886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, The 10 dot abilities of the ante's used to be described as late as 2nd edition, and they weren't even the out there. Powerful yeah, but powerful in the &quot;I can use a undead army to conquer New York&quot; or &quot;I can send vague dreams to the masses of sleeping people on the other side of the world&quot;, kind of powerful. They were not &quot;I can take on the combined might of humankind(or even just vampire-kind)&quot; level of powerful, which lined up neatly with the need for having a Masquerade in the first place. Making them into unknowable I-Win buttons for the ST, kind of forgets that little tidbit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in a bit of a devil's advocate defense of the &quot;\u00fcberpowerful world-breaking Antes&quot; camp, the assumption was already at least in part in the Storyteller's section of the 1e or 2e corebook, when it gives some NPC stats guidelines if memory tricks me not. &quot;Elder&quot; (lvl 6+) discipline powers would only come later in the Player's Guide (oh, the irony....) and even then it was kind of obvious a bunch of them were subpar to say the least. Nowadays i'd say 2/3 of them would be better off as discipline combos or standalone rituals in the 1-5 range.<br /> <br /> <br /> But speaking of higher level powers, one might say that reading Chicago by Night for the first time - the part about Menele and Pompeii in particular was something of a personal milestone and pretty much defined my concept of the power scale from that point forward.<br /> <br /> Aka the &quot;<i>if your thaumaturgy 7 power can't destroy a city in one scene, <b>you're doing it wrong</b></i>&quot; rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or in a (rough) reach table, inspired by the (older editions) Influence background's progression.<br /> Level 6 - city district or a whole town<br /> Level 7 - whole city<br /> Level 8 - american state [or european country]<br /> Level 9 - region [or group of countries like the british isles, scandinavia, arabian peninsula, etc]<br /> Level 10 - very large country/subcontinent [China, India, Brazil, Siberia, etc]<br /> <br /> It's anything but perfect i'll be the first to admit, but has been imensely helpful in giving me a framework within which to adjust official elder disciplines, NPC power level and other sundry things for my games across the decades.<br /> <br /> (Also the main reason i almost never use anything beyond 7th-6th gen in the table. Even my versions of many canonic ones) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-18-2022, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T11:24:08-08:00","id":1474914,"title":"","content":"I never equated the Antedeluvians to the scale of the Great Old Ones, but they were supposed to be supremely powerful when it comes to other vampires, and obviously that meant they were a risk to most other things on Earth. The original World of Darkness implied there was to be an end to the world - Gehenna, Apocalypse, Ascension, Doomsday, and Endless Winter were all essentially the same thing. The current world was going to be destroyed, but there was a chance for a new one to be born after the defeat of ultimate evil according to whatever eschatology the ST wanted. I always considered Gehenna to simply be one event during the Apocalypse that would lead to Doomsday. The Antedeluvians were likely to be destroyed at some point during the Apocalypse - just not by other vampires - but by other powerful beings who would have appeared during the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> If the Antedeluvians - remnants of a legendary world that was destroyed - exist like a Sword of Damocles hanging over the fates of every vampire on Earth, they are an interesting setting element. If they are just another powerful vampire, not so interesting. So while I would not use the same language of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> , I agree with her.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> As an aside, I laugh when people think the ending of the Call of Cthulhu implies Cthulhu isn't extremely powerful (and he isn't all powerful, he's simply the High Priest of his alien race). Cthulhu wasn't defeated at all. The steam powered ship - supreme technology of the 1920s when the story was written - could only temporarily disrupt him as he reformed immediately after. He was like a hibernating bear temporarily chasing away an intruder in his cave before going back to hibernation. The entire point of the story is that the stars are not right, not yet. There was just a minor conjunction that temporarily allowed a portion of Cthulhu's mind and might to influence the world which resulted in a series of death and madness. But I think Baldaam actually knows that and is just having fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T11:27:05-08:00","id":1474915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474893#post1474893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But speaking of higher level powers, one might say that reading Chicago by Night for the first time - the part about Menele and Pompeii in particular was something of a personal milestone and pretty much defined my concept of the power scale from that point forward.<br /> <br /> Aka the &quot;<i>if your thaumaturgy 7 power can't destroy a city in one scene, <b>you're doing it wrong</b></i>&quot; rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or in a (rough) reach table, inspired by the (older editions) Influence background's progression.<br /> Level 6 - city district or a whole town<br /> Level 7 - whole city<br /> Level 8 - american state [or european country]<br /> Level 9 - region [or group of countries like the british isles, scandinavia, arabian peninsula, etc]<br /> Level 10 - very large country/subcontinent [China, India, Brazil, Siberia, etc]<br /> <br /> It's anything but perfect i'll be the first to admit, but has been imensely helpful in giving me a framework within which to adjust official elder disciplines, NPC power level and other sundry things for my games across the decades.<br /> <br /> (Also the main reason i almost never use anything beyond 7th-6th gen in the table. Even my versions of many canonic ones) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I can See that, but I think that rule also needed an addendum saying that Thaum 7+(and other disciplines) need an added cost that makes using them frequently, and/or using them openly, a horrible idea.<br /> <br /> Even with limited numbers of elders, if they're All at-will nukes, then why haven't they openly conquered the world? What would they be afraid of besides each other?<br /> <br /> My person feeling on this is to lean into the Really Powerful disciplines having a cost that makes them more emergency-only, punishing to use frequently deals, or that they have Glaring Weaknesses.<br /> <br /> For example: Dominate 7 allowing you to control a large city and bend it to your will, but anyone who wears a holy symbol is immune to your power. There's a big reason why the a vampire with the example power wouldn't want himself or his power to come to light, as anyone with hands could make a cross or draw a pentacle in 30 seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T13:11:21-08:00","id":1474920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474914#post1474914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I laugh when people think the ending of the Call of Cthulhu implies Cthulhu isn't extremely powerful (and he isn't all powerful, he's simply the High Priest of his alien race). Cthulhu wasn't defeated at all. The steam powered ship - supreme technology of the 1920s when the story was written - could only temporarily disrupt him as he reformed immediately after. He was like a hibernating bear temporarily chasing away an intruder in his cave before going back to hibernation. The entire point of the story is that the stars are not right, not yet. There was just a minor conjunction that temporarily allowed a portion of Cthulhu's mind and might to influence the world which resulted in a series of death and madness. But I think Baldaam actually knows that and is just having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Came here to say this. There are examples of cosmic horror monsters being soundly defeated in Lovecraft -- &quot;The Dunwich Horror&quot; comes to mind -- but &quot;The Call of Cthulhu&quot; isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> I feel like the idea that cosmic horror monsters are &quot;supposed&quot; to be any one thing already goes astray. The Yog-Sothothery of Lovecraft and friends was never meant to be the internally consistent mythology that it's sometimes portrayed as in modern media, but only a set of shared story elements that individual authors could use and abuse to their liking.<br /> <br /> In the hands of Robert E. Howard, for example, eldritch horrors get punched in the face, as in &quot;The Slithering Shadow.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T17:09:37-08:00","id":1474928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474920#post1474920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Came here to say this. There are examples of cosmic horror monsters being soundly defeated in Lovecraft -- &quot;The Dunwich Horror&quot; comes to mind -- but &quot;The Call of Cthulhu&quot; isn't one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, a dark inevitable fate forestalled for a few generations at most - but that can be victory aplenty from the flawed perspective of mayfly fleshly human irrelevances, i dare say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474920#post1474920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the idea that cosmic horror monsters are &quot;supposed&quot; to be any one thing already goes astray. The Yog-Sothothery of Lovecraft and friends was never meant to be the internally consistent mythology that it's sometimes portrayed as in modern media, but only a set of shared story elements that individual authors could use and abuse to their liking.<br /> <br /> In the hands of Robert E. Howard, for example, eldritch horrors get punched in the face, as in &quot;The Slithering Shadow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's layers and layers to this for sure, even in Lovecraft's own yarns, as shown by the actions of <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Inspector Legrasse and Gustaf Johansen in &quot;Call of Cthulhu&quot;, the protagonists of </span></span></span>&quot;The Dunwich Horror&quot; as you cited, the federal intervention that frames the events in &quot;Shadow Over Innsmouth&quot; among other examples. Context, scale and the degree of awareness, preparedness &amp; mental fortitude of the parts involved, all of these may play a role in how things turn out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474915#post1474915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I can See that, but I think that rule also needed an addendum saying that Thaum 7+(and other disciplines) need an added cost that makes using them frequently, and/or using them openly, a horrible idea.<br /> <br /> Even with limited numbers of elders, if they're All at-will nukes, then why haven't they openly conquered the world? What would they be afraid of besides each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, being afraid of each other can be reason aplenty when your special powers can be quite the fireworks display pointing your presence and actions, specially when some of those have Auspex 5+, might be said. not to mention so uncommon that one specific elder power might end up being something of a identifying fingerprint for those acquainted with that particular ancient, directly or through indirect sources like past witnesses, written records, prophecies and so on.<br /> <br /> Also, i came up with this back when Under a Blood Red Moon was still novelty, so a number of years before <i>physical </i>disciplines gained elder effects of their own in VtDA, what created a sort of &quot;<i>Sephiroth and his world-destroying Meteor</i>&quot; uneveness between the physical and non-physical disciplines, one that might be exploited by lesser beings such as younger kindred, other supernaturals and even mortals, depending on circunstances, in a direct confrontation. I have added the extra powers for physical disciplines since, but as i just add book examples instead of trying to rescale, the uneveness still stands, what is useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474915#post1474915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My person feeling on this is to lean into the Really Powerful disciplines having a cost that makes them more emergency-only, punishing to use frequently deals, or that they have Glaring Weaknesses.<br /> <br /> For example: Dominate 7 allowing you to control a large city and bend it to your will, but anyone who wears a holy symbol is immune to your power. There's a big reason why the a vampire with the example power wouldn't want himself or his power to come to light, as anyone with hands could make a cross or draw a pentacle in 30 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have a point i agree and truth be told i <b>do</b> have some soft limiters - though laziness makes me dread going into the nitty-gritty of putting that stuff in posts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - but for the sake of reference, use of such powers has complications and risks of their own, in the form of cataclysmic botches (such as <i>Menele's summoning under frenzy</i> in Pompeii might be interpreted as) and the possibility of the individual being <i>overtaken by the power</i> in a frenzy-like trance state that could last from hours to days in which it would do who knows what else, something that could be worsened if the power was somehow &quot;inherited&quot; from past diablerie.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, &quot;just&quot; using discipline combos of 1-5 powers but with ludricous 11+ dice pools could be much more reliable and safe overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-08-2023, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T17:14:51-08:00","id":1474929,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a guy who has written Lovecraft fiction, one of the most clever things I ever read was an article that pointed out the universe is cold, hostile, and malevolent to humans in HPL.<br /> <br /> BUT it's also not necessarily friendlier to the Mythos.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T18:02:05-08:00","id":1474936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474929#post1474929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as a guy who has written Lovecraft fiction, one of the most clever things I ever read was an article that pointed out the universe is cold, hostile, and malevolent to humans in HPL.<br /> <br /> BUT it's also not necessarily friendlier to the Mythos.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A <i><b>very</b></i> fair point indeed and one i've toyed with at times in some pulpy dark fantasy games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-18-2022, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T22:23:06-08:00","id":1474946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474920#post1474920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the hands of Robert E. Howard, for example, eldritch horrors get punched in the face, as in &quot;The Slithering Shadow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Each of the Big Three of Weird Tales - Lovecraft, CAS, and Howard - had very different takes on the same concepts. Lovecraft being the stronger horror writer, Smith a fantasist, and Howard in heroic adventures. Smith wasn't even consistent in how he presented Tsathoggua - sometimes horrific, other times comical or even adorable. Although they would sometimes use the same concept and contributions of all three would find their way into the Call of Cthulhu RPG, I would say only Lovecraft wrote &quot;cosmic horror&quot; as it is usually defined. Howard could be a fantastic horror writer - Pigeons From Hell is a great horror story - but he used horror in a different way than Lovecraft did.<br /> <br /> Vampire has stronger roots in the Gothic Horror tradition so I lean more towards that in presenting the Antedeluvians than as something akin to the Great Old Ones. But in Werewolf, for example, I am more willing to go towards cosmic horror, although to use No One of Consequence's phrase it's like &quot;Conan versus the Mythos&quot; rather than Lovecraft's take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T01:10:36-08:00","id":1474949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474914#post1474914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never equated the Antedeluvians to the scale of the Great Old Ones, but they were supposed to be supremely powerful when it comes to other vampires, and obviously that meant they were a risk to most other things on Earth. The original World of Darkness implied there was to be an end to the world - Gehenna, Apocalypse, Ascension, Doomsday, and Endless Winter were all essentially the same thing. The current world was going to be destroyed, but there was a chance for a new one to be born after the defeat of ultimate evil according to whatever eschatology the ST wanted. I always considered Gehenna to simply be one event during the Apocalypse that would lead to Doomsday. The Antedeluvians were likely to be destroyed at some point during the Apocalypse - just not by other vampires - but by other powerful beings who would have appeared during the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> If the Antedeluvians - remnants of a legendary world that was destroyed - exist like a Sword of Damocles hanging over the fates of every vampire on Earth, they are an interesting setting element. If they are just another powerful vampire, not so interesting. So while I would not use the same language of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> , I agree with her.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> As an aside, I laugh when people think the ending of the Call of Cthulhu implies Cthulhu isn't extremely powerful (and he isn't all powerful, he's simply the High Priest of his alien race). Cthulhu wasn't defeated at all. The steam powered ship - supreme technology of the 1920s when the story was written - could only temporarily disrupt him as he reformed immediately after. He was like a hibernating bear temporarily chasing away an intruder in his cave before going back to hibernation. The entire point of the story is that the stars are not right, not yet. There was just a minor conjunction that temporarily allowed a portion of Cthulhu's mind and might to influence the world which resulted in a series of death and madness. But I think Baldaam actually knows that and is just having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I consider some dude with a boat ramming him so hard he exploded (for some reason) and got sucked back into the crypt until the next time the stars aligned correctly to be a loss. Sure Cthulhu wasn't dead but he suffered a major non-permanent set back that saw him deprived of freedom and sent back to having nothing to do but watch a bunch of dead gods be dead for another few eons. I'm sure he considered this to be fairly annoying on his end and very rude of the lesser creature that steam boated him before he had a chance to even really stretch his legs and get some fresh air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T01:15:40-08:00","id":1474950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474949#post1474949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I consider some dude with a boat ramming him so hard he exploded (for some reason) and got sucked back into the crypt until the next time the stars aligned correctly to be a loss. Sure Cthulhu wasn't dead but he suffered a major non-permanent set back that saw him deprived of freedom and sent back to having nothing to do but watch a bunch of dead gods be dead for another few eons. I'm sure he considered this to be fairly annoying on his end and very rude of the lesser creature that steam boated him before he had a chance to even really stretch his legs and get some fresh air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> The actual situation in <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> is a bit different and is more like Raiders of the Lost Ark than Temple of Doom (i.e. the protagonists accomplish nothing and it's all out of their hands): Cthulhu's cult is waiting for the stars to be right and are murdering people across the globe as they do rituals to summon him but the rituals are actually doing nothing as R'lyeh will rise entirely on its own and the reason Cthulhu's cult is having visions of their dark master is because Cthulhu is slowly waking up and he's a psychic on par with Professor X times 1000. Cthulhu wakes up and the protags proceed to drive the steamer ship through his skull and he's splattered around because he's not quite awake yet.<br /> <br /> They all celebrate....and then Cthulhu pulls himself back together like the T-1000, no worse for wear and the protags get the duck out of Fodge.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu then goes back to sleep because R'lyeh is sinking and it WASN'T the time for his rise.<br /> <br /> It was just CLOSE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-19-2022, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T01:32:35-08:00","id":1474951,"title":"","content":"To go with my earlier statements about the Antediluvians existing as a religion. The point is that they manage to establish a lot of the fear and supernatural dread that millennialist Christianity induces without having to really get into the specifics of apocalyptic Christianity.<br /> <br /> By what I mean:<br /> <br /> 1:] <b>The Antediluvians are going to rise eventually to kill you</b><br /> <br /> A vampire is immortal but the existence of Gehenna effectively means that their immortality is a lie. They can live for a year, ten years, a thousand years, or longer but when the Antediluvians rise up, they will destroy you and it will end. It is thus an existential fear of Elders and even Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> 2:] <b>The Antediluvians are mysterious</b><br /> <br /> The thing about the Antediluvians is they're usually spoken about as a group rather than the singular. When vampires think of Nosferatu, Toreador, or Ventrue then they have a personality but very few of them are people the Clan despises with exceptions like Nossie and Cappadocias. The Followers of Set and Haqimites exempted. There's not enough known about them for you to appease them and thus they induce more dread.<br /> <br /> 3:] <b>The Antediluvians make you feel like a victim</b><br /> <br /> The symbolism of cannibalism among the undead with diablerie is something that exists both in and out of universe. Vampires feed on humans and are terrifying to them. Humans are food, cattle, and slaves. There's thus no greater existential fear than being made into food and cattle by a vampire more powerful than you.<br /> <br /> 4:] <b>Weird cults offer you a way out</b><br /> <br /> The Book of Nod is something vampires turn to out of a desire to figure out a &quot;cheat&quot; for what is their inevitable Final Deaths. There are also weird cults like the kind in Forbidden Religion or the ENTIRE EXISTENCE of the Followers of Set and Banu Haqim that the Antediluvians can be appeased.<br /> <br /> 5:] <b>The Antediluvians are probably real. Probably</b><br /> <br /> I think it was a mistake to have Gehenna happen because part of the fun is that the Antediluvians can be completely misunderstood. The Dark Ages called a lot of the lore about them into question because Lasombra was up and about 1000 years ago without turning anyone into a meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T02:16:14-08:00","id":1474953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474951#post1474951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Ages called a lot of the lore about them into question because Lasombra was up and about 1000 years ago without turning anyone into a meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was always awkward to me. You had vampires like Lasombra, or Cappadocius or Saulot, or Brujah (Troile) were all engaged in activities and performing various actions, and weren't horrible blood thirsty monsters. So it kind of destroyed the mystique of Gehenna and called into question a lot of the concepts about Antediluvians, since we saw several &quot;on screen&quot; and they never acted like blood thirsty, childe-devouring ur-gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T08:32:45-08:00","id":1474980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474950#post1474950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite.<br /> <br /> The actual situation in <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> is a bit different and is more like Raiders of the Lost Ark than Temple of Doom (i.e. the protagonists accomplish nothing and it's all out of their hands): Cthulhu's cult is waiting for the stars to be right and are murdering people across the globe as they do rituals to summon him but the rituals are actually doing nothing as R'lyeh will rise entirely on its own and the reason Cthulhu's cult is having visions of their dark master is because Cthulhu is slowly waking up and he's a psychic on par with Professor X times 1000. Cthulhu wakes up and the protags proceed to drive the steamer ship through his skull and he's splattered around because he's not quite awake yet.<br /> <br /> They all celebrate....and then Cthulhu pulls himself back together like the T-1000, no worse for wear and the protags get the duck out of Fodge.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu then goes back to sleep because R'lyeh is sinking and it WASN'T the time for his rise.<br /> <br /> It was just CLOSE.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always had the impression that if he hadn't been distracted by getting his brains splattered he would have done something to affix it in place and it only fell again because he was stopped from having a chance to do anything. But it has been an extremely long time since I last read it so I might just not be remembering things properly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:28:30-08:00","id":1474988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474953#post1474953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was always awkward to me. You had vampires like Lasombra, or Cappadocius or Saulot, or Brujah (Troile) were all engaged in activities and performing various actions, and weren't horrible blood thirsty monsters. So it kind of destroyed the mystique of Gehenna and called into question a lot of the concepts about Antediluvians, since we saw several &quot;on screen&quot; and they never acted like blood thirsty, childe-devouring ur-gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they WERE horrible bloodthirsty monsters. I imagine every Antediluvian nest is akin to Caligula's court or Thulsa Doom's Mountain of Power. It's just they weren't up for the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Cappadocias: *cough*<br /> <br /> Well, you DID want to kill and eat God.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I think calling that into question was a feature not a bug. It made the skepticism about Gehenna make more sense. Besides, it also illuminated just how long the Antediluvians had been around that Mithras is probably a younger childe of theirs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-19-2022, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:36:35-08:00","id":1474989,"title":"","content":"Didn't Cappadocius cull like 50% of his clan after testing to see who the dumbest most gullible 50% were just because he was annoyed at how large his clan became? He doesn't seem like a good example to use for 'why is everybody so worried about these guys coming back and killing a bunch of their descendants some of them were cool'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-19-2022, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T19:38:50-08:00","id":1475014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474989#post1474989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Cappadocius cull like 50% of his clan after testing to see who the dumbest most gullible 50% were just because he was annoyed at how large his clan became? He doesn't seem like a good example to use for 'why is everybody so worried about these guys coming back and killing a bunch of their descendants some of them were cool'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never understood this because the Cappadocians act like this is a heinous act when getting rid of the worst of a clan seems like something a responsible Antediluvian SHOULD do.<br /> <br /> It's also hard to think most vampires would mind the culling of their ranks because the people who hate vampires most are other vampires.<br /> <br /> It's also apparently the Cycle of Gehenna in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> 1. Embrace a bunch of vampires<br /> 2. Go to sleep<br /> 3. Wake up and eat 90% of your descendants<br /> 4. Embrace a bunch of vampires<br /> 5. Go to sleep<br /> <br /> Why there's 4th generation only a couple of thousand years old and not hundreds from the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T22:45:45-08:00","id":1475018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474949#post1474949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I consider some dude with a boat ramming him so hard he exploded (for some reason) and got sucked back into the crypt until the next time the stars aligned correctly to be a loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I fired a gun at someone, and that person temporarily turned into mist so the bullet wouldn't hit him, and then reformed, I wouldn't consider that I exploded the guy. I would consider my attempt to kill him to be a failure and be absolutely terrified.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474949#post1474949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure Cthulhu wasn't dead but he suffered a major non-permanent set back that saw him deprived of freedom and sent back to having nothing to do but watch a bunch of dead gods be dead for another few eons.</div> </div> </div> </div>From Cthulhu's perspective, it isn't major. He just went back to sleep. The reason why he temporarily woke up and went back to sleep had nothing to do with humanity. It had to do with forces beyond mankind's control. And we don't even know whether Cthulhu's slumber is anything like a prison. It might simply be a natural cycle for his race.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474949#post1474949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure he considered this to be fairly annoying on his end and very rude of the lesser creature that steam boated him before he had a chance to even really stretch his legs and get some fresh air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Annoying and rude maybe, like a fly landing on your nose while you slumber, and you swat it away while still being half-asleep.<br /> <br /> If that's your interpretation of the story, OK. But I don't think it's what the most readers believe, or that it was Lovecraft's intent. The story literally ends with the narrator fearing not just for mankind, but that the Cthulhu cultists will soon find and murder him.<br /> <br /> But this is getting us further from the actual subject of the thread which is the use of Antedeluvians in Vampire, not a discussion of the Great Old Ones in Lovecraft's stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T23:20:08-08:00","id":1475019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1475014#post1475014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never understood this because the Cappadocians act like this is a heinous act when getting rid of the worst of a clan seems like something a responsible Antediluvian SHOULD do.<br /> <br /> It's also hard to think most vampires would mind the culling of their ranks because the people who hate vampires most are other vampires.<br /> <br /> It's also apparently the Cycle of Gehenna in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> 1. Embrace a bunch of vampires<br /> 2. Go to sleep<br /> 3. Wake up and eat 90% of your descendants<br /> 4. Embrace a bunch of vampires<br /> 5. Go to sleep<br /> <br /> Why there's 4th generation only a couple of thousand years old and not hundreds from the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably they considered it his own fault for not paying attention to the quantity or quality of his clan's growth until someone pointed out there were now so many of them they were about to literally bleed their stronghold cities dry and implode. Nobody appreciates it when the boss screws up then makes it somebody elses problem without even putting any of their own skin in the game to fix it. And the way he killed them was a pretty huge dick move, he could of at least made it quick.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know, he could have just always told some of them to just move out of the damn nest instead of living in their Antediluvian's personal nest area instead of forcing them into a cannibal dinner party battle royal with the reward being a likely eternal torpor. Instead he actively called back even the ones who weren't bleeding the nest dry back to participate in the family dinner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-20-2022, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T01:13:57-08:00","id":1475022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1474988#post1474988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they WERE horrible bloodthirsty monsters. I imagine every Antediluvian nest is akin to Caligula's court or Thulsa Doom's Mountain of Power. It's just they weren't up for the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Cappadocias: *cough*<br /> <br /> Well, you DID want to kill and eat God.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I think calling that into question was a feature not a bug. It made the skepticism about Gehenna make more sense. Besides, it also illuminated just how long the Antediluvians had been around that Mithras is probably a younger childe of theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Cappadocius ends up having plans ruined and dies. Twice. Like some sort of bumblefuck Mr. Bean. My takeaway from all that was that the Antediluvians aren't nearly as powerful, intelligent, dangerous or undefeatable as the hype would lead people to believe. People who don't know any better would be worried about Gehenna and the Antidiluvians, but as players who have access to the meta-content of the game line, we all know better. I think that's why they ended up going in the opposite direction with Ravnos and had him only defeated by ancient kung-fu vampires and space lasers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-20-2022, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T01:35:24-08:00","id":1475024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1475022#post1475022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Cappadocius ends up having plan ruined and dies. Twice. Like some sort of bumblefuck Mr. Bean. My takeaway from all that was that the Antediluvians aren't nearly as powerful, intelligent, dangerous or undefeatable as the hype would lead people to believe. People who don't know any better would be worried about Gehenna and the Antidiluvians, but as players who have access to the meta-content of the game line, we all know better. I think that's why they ended up going in the opposite direction with Ravnos and had him only defeated by ancient kung-fu vampires and space lasers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And magical nukes that rent the veil between worlds and triggered major spirit realm repercussions, don't forget that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T05:43:36-08:00","id":1475033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1475024#post1475024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And magical nukes that rent the veil between worlds and triggered major spirit realm repercussions, don't forget that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Cappadocias is much better off because Cappadocias at least was lucid. His plan was nuts but there was a plan.<br /> <br /> Ravnos woke up and frenzied until dead.<br /> <br /> I always liked the idea they could become wights as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T05:58:47-08:00","id":1475035,"title":"","content":"My opinion:<br /> <br /> 1. It is hard to write a millennium old ex-human creature mentality. <br /> 2. VtR writers were not exactly Pulitzer prize winners themselves, lacking real world knowledge (very USA-centric + blatant stupidities like the &quot;asians are special therefore special vampires for them&quot;, and the abomination of Wod-Gypsies book among others)<br /> 3. Mechanical issues also made the story inconsistent (only 15 generations of Vampires from the dawn of human civilization to now???)<br /> <br /> <br /> All those points give you an inconsistent lore, so your best bet is to make Antes mysterious as the Gehenna book tries to be (not stating them directly, treating them as plot devices) so the story drives the plot, not these crazy Attribute 10 + Discipline 10 + Billion of combination disciplines stat sets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T06:09:41-08:00","id":1475037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1475035#post1475035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion:<br /> <br /> 3. Mechanical issues also made the story inconsistent (only 15 generations of Vampires from the dawn of human civilization to now???)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That part is actually very clever because the &quot;weakning of blood&quot; means vampires always have to be Embracing and diablerizing each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T18:05:15-08:00","id":1475067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1475033#post1475033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Cappadocias is much better off because Cappadocias at least was lucid. His plan was nuts but there was a plan.<br /> <br /> Ravnos woke up and frenzied until dead.<br /> <br /> I always liked the idea they could become wights as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, Cappadocius turned into a wraith and then got overtaken by his Shadow. That meant that while &quot;Cappadocius&quot; was lucid, he was also essentially reduced to being a tiny voice in Spectre Cappadocius' mind, trapped and forced to watch all of the things Spectre Cappadocius was doing but unable to take any actions or change the outcome in any way. It's pretty arguable if that's &quot;better&quot; than being in a state of frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T21:06:55-08:00","id":1475081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/938911-antedeluvian-power-level?p=1475022#post1475022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My takeaway from all that was that the Antediluvians aren't nearly as powerful, intelligent, dangerous or undefeatable as the hype would lead people to believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually how I personally run the Antes, and I think some of the blunders make for better story elements than the whole god-like powers and shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Looking at them, there are a number of ways in which an Ante can affect a story:<br /> <br /> 1 - Be the focus of cult/religion/legend;<br /> 2 - Influence events and people as ultimate string-pullers;<br /> 3 - Leave behind the aftereffects of their shenanigans;<br /> 4 - Actually show up, but not to put up a fight;<br /> 5 - Final Boss Mode.<br /> <br /> None of those is superior or inferior, they all can be done well or badly, so their ideal power depends on what you want to take of it.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: most people like to work with #1 and #2, and so make their legend as true as possible. <i>But that's completely unnecessary</i>. Here's some considerations:<br /> <br /> 1 - The truth of the matter seems important because of the characters that so strongly believe in it, but it actually isn't. What people do with their beliefs is far more important than those beliefs being right, and being in the wrong here is not a sign of being dumb, as the characters live inside the setting, without the outside perspective there's no reason for them to know <u><b>the</b></u> truth;<br /> <br /> 2 - Personal power is irrelevant as what matters is the thread of manipulation. In this regard I actually find the notion of god-like powers over their progeny more of a bug than a feature. This sort of Super-Dominate leaves no meaningful threads to be explored and no way to interact with their plot, as anything you do is either a part of it or unable to affect it and ultimately irrelevant. The notion that god-like ancestors may be causing everyone's thoughts and actions is interesting and terrifying, but while it seems to be #2, ultimately is actually #1;<br /> <br /> 3 - Ancient vampires do not need god-like powers to leave behind god-like marks. Any number of factors may affect a given context to make the actions of someone there have huge proportions. They could have taken their time, used a powerful artifact, used combined power of many others, just because they left what appears to be the ruins of an impossibly big fortress of pure obsidian that legend says the Ancient built alone in a single night, it doesn't mean any of those is individually true;<br /> <br /> 4 - Here the more alien or powerful the character, the less options you have to actually build an interesting interaction. A protean, ninety stories high monstrosity that knows in details each animal on the planet due to its mastery of Vicissitude and is about to choose and eat everyone without hope of resistance is terrifying. But is also just as meaningful as a big enough meteor, that is, a falling rock; Meaning exists within boundaries, so your Ancient should be weak enough to not threaten your story's boundaries.<br /> <br /> 5 - You only have a meaningful benefit from a too big power level when you want the characters to put up a fight and be completely overpowered, or to highlight how much power they accrued in their bid to try and face gods. If you don't want any of those two specific things in your story, though, then by necessity it must be weak enough to work for the fight you actually intend to.<br /> <br /> Caveat: Cosmic Horror is a fun genre, but a specific one. But even in it, while the characters face evidence that the power level of the Unspeakable Things is indeed too high, the actual story works mostly with #1, #2 or #3. Few of them use #4 and they don't have a lot of meaningful interaction (Call of Cthulhu), or they use #4 but the entity is limited, if not in actual power, in its willingness to exhibit that power, making it effectively less powerful in the actual context of the story (almost anything with Nyarlathotep).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}